-- Social Security (Personal Independence Payment) Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/377) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: the person to whom the Regulations are applied: someone aged 16 or over with a health condition or
-- disability who claims, or receives, personal independence payment.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules of the modules imported above as the questions that person asks: what my
-- descriptors score, whether I have limited or severely limited ability, whether I meet the required period
-- condition, whether I satisfy the residence and presence conditions on a day, what I am paid a week, whether
-- I can keep my payment after the relevant age, and whether I am paid while I am in a care home, a hospital or
-- custody. Nothing here is new law: each question builds the module's own records from plain answers and calls
-- the module's own rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs, yes/no, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices, one for each
-- fact the person states, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. A date that may not exist (the
-- day I applied, the day the Secretary of State certified) is a yes/no and a date; the record is built inside the
-- question. A question that needs the answer to another question (for example, whether regulation 23 applies to
-- me) takes it as a yes/no and says in its @desc which question gives it.
--
-- WHAT THE SEAT DOES NOT DECIDE. The judgments the Regulations hand to the Secretary of State are asked as the
-- person's best statement of them and never guessed: whether it is likely that the Secretary of State would
-- determine a level of ability (regs 12 and 13), whether the Secretary of State is satisfied that C had good
-- reason (regs 8(3), 9(2)), that it is unreasonable to expect C to return (reg 18A), or that the entitlement
-- results from the same condition (reg 15(1)(d)). The Act's own terms (the relevant age, terminally ill, a
-- relevant EU Regulation, a care home) are asked as facts.
--
-- READINGS ASSUMED, NOT RULED (see the fork register of NOTES.md):
--   * The number of years in regulation 15(1)(b) and 15B(1)(b) is 1 for a person who has reached the relevant age
--     and 2 for a person who has not (regulations 26(2)(b) and 26A(2)(b)); regulation 26(1) refers to "the
--     circumstances set out in regulation 15" and regulation 15(1)(b) depends on regulation 26 (fork F-39).
--   * Both versions of regulation 23A(1)(i), (j) and (k), (l), and both versions of regulation 27(2), are
--     applied to the same answers; a person is covered if either version covers them (forks F-24, F-32).
--   * Where regulation 23ZA meets regulation 20, 23 or 23A(1A) the text does not say which prevails, and the answer
--     "the text does not say" is returned, not a guess (fork F-22).

§ `Social Security (Personal Independence Payment) Regulations 2013 -- the questions a claimant asks`

DECLARE `which required period applies to me` IS ONE OF
    `a claim made after an interval, under regulation 15 or 15A`
    `any other claim`
    `a day of my award in the 3 months after such a claim`
    `a day of my award in any other case`

-- The row of Schedule 1 for an activity and the letter of a descriptor in it: the person names the descriptor by its
-- activity and its letter, and the modules find the row by the descriptor's own type.
GIVEN a IS AN `an activity of Schedule 1`
      l IS A `a letter of a descriptor`
GIVETH A MAYBE `a row of Schedule 1`
`seat: the row of Schedule 1 for the activity and letter` a l MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD (r's `its activity`) EQUALS a AND (r's `its letter`) EQUALS l)
                    (append (`all the rows of the daily living activities table`) (`all the rows of the mobility activities table`))
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST r

GIVEN a IS AN `an activity of Schedule 1`
      l IS A `a letter of a descriptor`
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
`seat: the descriptor of the activity with this letter, satisfied on this many days` a l `on` d MEANS
    CONSIDER `seat: the row of Schedule 1 for the activity and letter` a l
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (`a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF r, d)

-- A letter that names no descriptor of the activity (for example letter g of mobility activity 2) cannot be scored. Where days are
-- given for it, the question returns NOTHING, not a score worked out from the other descriptors alone.
GIVEN a IS AN `an activity of Schedule 1`
      l IS A `a letter of a descriptor`
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`seat: the letter names no descriptor of the activity although days are given` a l d MEANS
        d GREATER THAN 0
    AND (NOT (isJust (`seat: the row of Schedule 1 for the activity and letter` a l)))

§§ `The assessment: descriptors, points and levels of ability (Part 2)`

-- reg 7(1), Schedule 1. The descriptor that applies to an activity is the one satisfied on over 50% of the days of the
-- required period; if more than one, the one that scores more; if none, the one satisfied for most days among the
-- descriptors that together are satisfied on over 50% of the days. The question takes up to three descriptors.
@export How many points do I score for this activity, from the days on which each descriptor applies to me (reg 7(1))?
GIVEN `the activity` IS AN `an activity of Schedule 1` @desc Which activity of Schedule 1 is this? (daily living activities 1 to 10, mobility activities 1 and 2)
      `the letter of my first descriptor` IS A `a letter of a descriptor` @desc What is the letter of the first descriptor of this activity that applies to you on some days? (a to g)
      `the days on which my first descriptor applies` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days of your required period would you satisfy that first descriptor? (0 if you do not use this one)
      `the letter of my second descriptor` IS A `a letter of a descriptor` @desc What is the letter of the second descriptor that applies to you on some days?
      `the days on which my second descriptor applies` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days of your required period would you satisfy the second descriptor? (0 if you do not use this one)
      `the letter of my third descriptor` IS A `a letter of a descriptor` @desc What is the letter of the third descriptor that applies to you on some days?
      `the days on which my third descriptor applies` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days of your required period would you satisfy the third descriptor? (0 if you do not use this one)
      `the days in my required period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are there in your required period? (see the question about the required period; usually 365)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many points do I score for this activity` IS
    IF     `seat: the letter names no descriptor of the activity although days are given` `the activity` `the letter of my first descriptor` `the days on which my first descriptor applies`
        OR `seat: the letter names no descriptor of the activity although days are given` `the activity` `the letter of my second descriptor` `the days on which my second descriptor applies`
        OR `seat: the letter names no descriptor of the activity although days are given` `the activity` `the letter of my third descriptor` `the days on which my third descriptor applies`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `reg 7(1): the descriptor which applies to C in relation to the activity` `my descriptors` `of` `the days in my required period`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `its points`)
    WHERE
        `my descriptors` MEANS
            mapMaybe (GIVEN x YIELD x)
                (LIST `seat: the descriptor of the activity with this letter, satisfied on this many days` `the activity` `the letter of my first descriptor` `on` `the days on which my first descriptor applies`
                    , `seat: the descriptor of the activity with this letter, satisfied on this many days` `the activity` `the letter of my second descriptor` `on` `the days on which my second descriptor applies`
                    , `seat: the descriptor of the activity with this letter, satisfied on this many days` `the activity` `the letter of my third descriptor` `on` `the days on which my third descriptor applies`)

-- reg 5(1), (2). The score is the sum of the points of the descriptor that applies to me for each of the ten daily
-- living activities. If regulation 7 selects none for an activity, the text does not say what the score is.
@export What is my score for daily living activities (reg 5(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my descriptor for preparing food` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 1` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for preparing food? Choose one: 1a: Can prepare and cook a simple meal unaided (0 points); 1b: Needs to use an aid or appliance to be able to either prepare or cook a simple meal (2 points); 1c: Cannot cook a simple meal using a conventional cooker but is able to do so using a microwave (2 points); 1d: Needs prompting to be able to either prepare or cook a simple meal (2 points); 1e: Needs supervision or assistance to either prepare or cook a simple meal (4 points); 1f: Cannot prepare and cook food (8 points)
      `my descriptor for taking nutrition` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 2` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for taking nutrition? Choose one: 2a: Can take nutrition unaided (0 points); 2b: Needs –(i) to use an aid or appliance to be able to take nutrition; or(ii) supervision to be able to take nutrition; or(iii) assistance to be able to cut up food (2 points); 2c: Needs a therapeutic source to be able to take nutrition (2 points); 2d: Needs prompting to be able to take nutrition (4 points); 2e: Needs assistance to be able to manage a therapeutic source to take nutrition (6 points); 2f: Cannot convey food and drink to their mouth and needs another person to do so (10 points)
      `my descriptor for managing therapy or monitoring a health condition` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 3` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for managing therapy or monitoring a health condition? Choose one: 3a: Either –(i) does not receive medication or therapy or need to monitor a health condition; or(ii) can manage medication or therapy or monitor a health condition unaided (0 points); 3b: Needs any one or more of the following –(i) to use an aid or appliance to be able to manage medication; ...(ii) supervision, prompting or assistance to be able to manage medication .... (iii) supervision, prompting or assistance to be able to monitor a health condition (1 points); 3c: Needs supervision, prompting or assistance to be able to manage therapy that takes no more than 3.5 hours a week (2 points); 3d: Needs supervision, prompting or assistance to be able to manage therapy that takes more than 3.5 but no more than 7 hours a week (4 points); 3e: Needs supervision, prompting or assistance to be able to manage therapy that takes more than 7 but no more than 14 hours a week (6 points); 3f: Needs supervision, prompting or assistance to be able to manage therapy that takes more than 14 hours a week (8 points)
      `my descriptor for washing and bathing` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 4` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for washing and bathing? Choose one: 4a: Can wash and bathe unaided (0 points); 4b: Needs to use an aid or appliance to be able to wash or bathe (2 points); 4c: Needs supervision or prompting to be able to wash or bathe (2 points); 4d: Needs assistance to be able to wash either their hair or body below the waist (2 points); 4e: Needs assistance to be able to get in or out of a bath or shower (3 points); 4f: Needs assistance to be able to wash their body between the shoulders and waist (4 points); 4g: Cannot wash and bathe at all and needs another person to wash their entire body (8 points)
      `my descriptor for managing toilet needs or incontinence` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 5` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for managing toilet needs or incontinence? Choose one: 5a: Can manage toilet needs or incontinence unaided (0 points); 5b: Needs to use an aid or appliance to be able to manage toilet needs or incontinence (2 points); 5c: Needs supervision or prompting to be able to manage toilet needs (2 points); 5d: Needs assistance to be able to manage toilet needs (4 points); 5e: Needs assistance to be able to manage incontinence of either bladder or bowel (6 points); 5f: Needs assistance to be able to manage incontinence of both bladder and bowel (8 points)
      `my descriptor for dressing and undressing` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 6` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for dressing and undressing? Choose one: 6a: Can dress and undress unaided (0 points); 6b: Needs to use an aid or appliance to be able to dress or undress (2 points); 6c: Needs either -(i) prompting to be able to dress, undress or determine appropriate circumstances for remaining clothed; or(ii) prompting or assistance to be able to select appropriate clothing (2 points); 6d: Needs assistance to be able to dress or undress their lower body (2 points); 6e: Needs assistance to be able to dress or undress their upper body (4 points); 6f: Cannot dress or undress at all (8 points)
      `my descriptor for communicating verbally` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 7` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for communicating verbally? Choose one: 7a: Can express and understand verbal information unaided (0 points); 7b: Needs to use an aid or appliance to be able to speak or hear (2 points); 7c: Needs communication support to be able to express or understand complex verbal information (4 points); 7d: Needs communication support to be able to express or understand basic verbal information (8 points); 7e: Cannot express or understand verbal information at all even with communication support (12 points)
      `my descriptor for reading and understanding signs, symbols and words` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 8` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for reading and understanding signs, symbols and words? Choose one: 8a: Can read and understand basic and complex written information either unaided or using spectacles or contact lenses (0 points); 8b: Needs to use an aid or appliance, other than spectacles or contact lenses, to be able to read or understand either basic or complex written information (2 points); 8c: Needs prompting to be able to read or understand complex written information (2 points); 8d: Needs prompting to be able to read or understand basic written information (4 points); 8e: Cannot read or understand signs, symbols or words at all (8 points)
      `my descriptor for engaging with other people face to face` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 9` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for engaging with other people face to face? Choose one: 9a: Can engage with other people unaided (0 points); 9b: Needs prompting to be able to engage with other people (2 points); 9c: Needs social support to be able to engage with other people (4 points); 9d: Cannot engage with other people due to such engagement causing either –(i) overwhelming psychological distress to the claimant; or(ii) the claimant to exhibit behaviour which would result in a substantial risk of harm to the claimant or another person (8 points)
      `my descriptor for making budgeting decisions` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 10` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for making budgeting decisions? Choose one: 10a: Can manage complex budgeting decisions unaided (0 points); 10b: Needs prompting or assistance to be able to make complex budgeting decisions (2 points); 10c: Needs prompting or assistance to be able to make simple budgeting decisions (4 points); 10d: Cannot make any budgeting decisions at all (6 points)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my score for daily living activities` IS
    `reg 5(1): the score C obtains in daily living activities` `my daily living descriptors`
    WHERE
        `my daily living descriptors` MEANS `the descriptors that apply to C in the daily living activities` WITH
            `for preparing food` IS `my descriptor for preparing food`
            `for taking nutrition` IS `my descriptor for taking nutrition`
            `for managing therapy or monitoring a health condition` IS `my descriptor for managing therapy or monitoring a health condition`
            `for washing and bathing` IS `my descriptor for washing and bathing`
            `for managing toilet needs or incontinence` IS `my descriptor for managing toilet needs or incontinence`
            `for dressing and undressing` IS `my descriptor for dressing and undressing`
            `for communicating verbally` IS `my descriptor for communicating verbally`
            `for reading and understanding signs, symbols and words` IS `my descriptor for reading and understanding signs, symbols and words`
            `for engaging with other people face to face` IS `my descriptor for engaging with other people face to face`
            `for making budgeting decisions` IS `my descriptor for making budgeting decisions`

-- reg 4(1), 5(3), 4(3). A score of at least 8 is limited ability, at least 12 is severely limited ability (and not also
-- limited), where I have undergone an assessment; the level is mine only if it results from my physical or mental condition.
@export Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities (regs 4(1), 4(3), 5(3))?
GIVEN `I have undergone an assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you undergone an assessment?
      `my limited ability results from my physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your difficulty with these activities result from your physical or mental condition?
      `my descriptor for preparing food` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 1` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for preparing food? Choose one: 1a: Can prepare and cook a simple meal unaided (0 points); 1b: Needs to use an aid or appliance to be able to either prepare or cook a simple meal (2 points); 1c: Cannot cook a simple meal using a conventional cooker but is able to do so using a microwave (2 points); 1d: Needs prompting to be able to either prepare or cook a simple meal (2 points); 1e: Needs supervision or assistance to either prepare or cook a simple meal (4 points); 1f: Cannot prepare and cook food (8 points)
      `my descriptor for taking nutrition` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 2` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for taking nutrition? Choose one: 2a: Can take nutrition unaided (0 points); 2b: Needs –(i) to use an aid or appliance to be able to take nutrition; or(ii) supervision to be able to take nutrition; or(iii) assistance to be able to cut up food (2 points); 2c: Needs a therapeutic source to be able to take nutrition (2 points); 2d: Needs prompting to be able to take nutrition (4 points); 2e: Needs assistance to be able to manage a therapeutic source to take nutrition (6 points); 2f: Cannot convey food and drink to their mouth and needs another person to do so (10 points)
      `my descriptor for managing therapy or monitoring a health condition` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 3` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for managing therapy or monitoring a health condition? Choose one: 3a: Either –(i) does not receive medication or therapy or need to monitor a health condition; or(ii) can manage medication or therapy or monitor a health condition unaided (0 points); 3b: Needs any one or more of the following –(i) to use an aid or appliance to be able to manage medication; ...(ii) supervision, prompting or assistance to be able to manage medication .... (iii) supervision, prompting or assistance to be able to monitor a health condition (1 points); 3c: Needs supervision, prompting or assistance to be able to manage therapy that takes no more than 3.5 hours a week (2 points); 3d: Needs supervision, prompting or assistance to be able to manage therapy that takes more than 3.5 but no more than 7 hours a week (4 points); 3e: Needs supervision, prompting or assistance to be able to manage therapy that takes more than 7 but no more than 14 hours a week (6 points); 3f: Needs supervision, prompting or assistance to be able to manage therapy that takes more than 14 hours a week (8 points)
      `my descriptor for washing and bathing` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 4` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for washing and bathing? Choose one: 4a: Can wash and bathe unaided (0 points); 4b: Needs to use an aid or appliance to be able to wash or bathe (2 points); 4c: Needs supervision or prompting to be able to wash or bathe (2 points); 4d: Needs assistance to be able to wash either their hair or body below the waist (2 points); 4e: Needs assistance to be able to get in or out of a bath or shower (3 points); 4f: Needs assistance to be able to wash their body between the shoulders and waist (4 points); 4g: Cannot wash and bathe at all and needs another person to wash their entire body (8 points)
      `my descriptor for managing toilet needs or incontinence` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 5` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for managing toilet needs or incontinence? Choose one: 5a: Can manage toilet needs or incontinence unaided (0 points); 5b: Needs to use an aid or appliance to be able to manage toilet needs or incontinence (2 points); 5c: Needs supervision or prompting to be able to manage toilet needs (2 points); 5d: Needs assistance to be able to manage toilet needs (4 points); 5e: Needs assistance to be able to manage incontinence of either bladder or bowel (6 points); 5f: Needs assistance to be able to manage incontinence of both bladder and bowel (8 points)
      `my descriptor for dressing and undressing` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 6` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for dressing and undressing? Choose one: 6a: Can dress and undress unaided (0 points); 6b: Needs to use an aid or appliance to be able to dress or undress (2 points); 6c: Needs either -(i) prompting to be able to dress, undress or determine appropriate circumstances for remaining clothed; or(ii) prompting or assistance to be able to select appropriate clothing (2 points); 6d: Needs assistance to be able to dress or undress their lower body (2 points); 6e: Needs assistance to be able to dress or undress their upper body (4 points); 6f: Cannot dress or undress at all (8 points)
      `my descriptor for communicating verbally` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 7` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for communicating verbally? Choose one: 7a: Can express and understand verbal information unaided (0 points); 7b: Needs to use an aid or appliance to be able to speak or hear (2 points); 7c: Needs communication support to be able to express or understand complex verbal information (4 points); 7d: Needs communication support to be able to express or understand basic verbal information (8 points); 7e: Cannot express or understand verbal information at all even with communication support (12 points)
      `my descriptor for reading and understanding signs, symbols and words` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 8` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for reading and understanding signs, symbols and words? Choose one: 8a: Can read and understand basic and complex written information either unaided or using spectacles or contact lenses (0 points); 8b: Needs to use an aid or appliance, other than spectacles or contact lenses, to be able to read or understand either basic or complex written information (2 points); 8c: Needs prompting to be able to read or understand complex written information (2 points); 8d: Needs prompting to be able to read or understand basic written information (4 points); 8e: Cannot read or understand signs, symbols or words at all (8 points)
      `my descriptor for engaging with other people face to face` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 9` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for engaging with other people face to face? Choose one: 9a: Can engage with other people unaided (0 points); 9b: Needs prompting to be able to engage with other people (2 points); 9c: Needs social support to be able to engage with other people (4 points); 9d: Cannot engage with other people due to such engagement causing either –(i) overwhelming psychological distress to the claimant; or(ii) the claimant to exhibit behaviour which would result in a substantial risk of harm to the claimant or another person (8 points)
      `my descriptor for making budgeting decisions` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 10` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for making budgeting decisions? Choose one: 10a: Can manage complex budgeting decisions unaided (0 points); 10b: Needs prompting or assistance to be able to make complex budgeting decisions (2 points); 10c: Needs prompting or assistance to be able to make simple budgeting decisions (4 points); 10d: Cannot make any budgeting decisions at all (6 points)
GIVETH A MAYBE `a level of ability to carry out activities`
DECIDE `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities` IS
    CONSIDER `reg 5(3): C's level of ability to carry out daily living activities` `I have undergone an assessment` (`reg 5(1): the score C obtains in daily living activities` `my daily living descriptors`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST level THEN JUST (`reg 4(1): C's level of ability, on the basis of an assessment` level `my limited ability results from my physical or mental condition`)
    WHERE
        `my daily living descriptors` MEANS `the descriptors that apply to C in the daily living activities` WITH
            `for preparing food` IS `my descriptor for preparing food`
            `for taking nutrition` IS `my descriptor for taking nutrition`
            `for managing therapy or monitoring a health condition` IS `my descriptor for managing therapy or monitoring a health condition`
            `for washing and bathing` IS `my descriptor for washing and bathing`
            `for managing toilet needs or incontinence` IS `my descriptor for managing toilet needs or incontinence`
            `for dressing and undressing` IS `my descriptor for dressing and undressing`
            `for communicating verbally` IS `my descriptor for communicating verbally`
            `for reading and understanding signs, symbols and words` IS `my descriptor for reading and understanding signs, symbols and words`
            `for engaging with other people face to face` IS `my descriptor for engaging with other people face to face`
            `for making budgeting decisions` IS `my descriptor for making budgeting decisions`

-- reg 6(1), (2). The score for the two mobility activities.
@export What is my score for mobility activities (reg 6(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my descriptor for planning and following journeys` IS A `a descriptor of mobility activity 1` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for planning and following journeys? Choose one: 1a: Can plan and follow the route of a journey unaided (0 points); 1b: Needs prompting to be able to undertake any journey to avoid overwhelming psychological distress to the claimant (4 points); 1c: Cannot plan the route of a journey (8 points); 1d: Cannot follow the route of an unfamiliar journey without another person, assistance dog or orientation aid (10 points); 1e: Cannot undertake any journey because it would cause overwhelming psychological distress to the claimant (10 points); 1f: Cannot follow the route of a familiar journey without another person, an assistance dog or an orientation aid (12 points)
      `my descriptor for moving around` IS A `a descriptor of mobility activity 2` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for moving around? Choose one: 2a: Can stand and then move more than 200 metres, either aided or unaided (0 points); 2b: Can stand and then move more than 50 metres but no more than 200 metres, either aided or unaided (4 points); 2c: Can stand and then move unaided more than 20 metres but no more than 50 metres (8 points); 2d: Can stand and then move using an aid or appliance more than 20 metres but no more than 50 metres (10 points); 2e: Can stand and then move more than 1 metre but no more than 20 metres, either aided or unaided (12 points); 2f: Cannot, either aided or unaided, –(i) stand; or(ii) move more than 1 metre (12 points)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my score for mobility activities` IS
    `reg 6(1): the score C obtains in mobility activities` `my mobility descriptors`
    WHERE
        `my mobility descriptors` MEANS `the descriptors that apply to C in the mobility activities` WITH
            `for planning and following journeys` IS `my descriptor for planning and following journeys`
            `for moving around` IS `my descriptor for moving around`

-- reg 4(1), 6(3), 4(3): the same thresholds for mobility activities.
@export Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out mobility activities (regs 4(1), 4(3), 6(3))?
GIVEN `I have undergone an assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you undergone an assessment?
      `my limited ability results from my physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your difficulty with these activities result from your physical or mental condition?
      `my descriptor for planning and following journeys` IS A `a descriptor of mobility activity 1` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for planning and following journeys? Choose one: 1a: Can plan and follow the route of a journey unaided (0 points); 1b: Needs prompting to be able to undertake any journey to avoid overwhelming psychological distress to the claimant (4 points); 1c: Cannot plan the route of a journey (8 points); 1d: Cannot follow the route of an unfamiliar journey without another person, assistance dog or orientation aid (10 points); 1e: Cannot undertake any journey because it would cause overwhelming psychological distress to the claimant (10 points); 1f: Cannot follow the route of a familiar journey without another person, an assistance dog or an orientation aid (12 points)
      `my descriptor for moving around` IS A `a descriptor of mobility activity 2` @desc Which descriptor applies to you for moving around? Choose one: 2a: Can stand and then move more than 200 metres, either aided or unaided (0 points); 2b: Can stand and then move more than 50 metres but no more than 200 metres, either aided or unaided (4 points); 2c: Can stand and then move unaided more than 20 metres but no more than 50 metres (8 points); 2d: Can stand and then move using an aid or appliance more than 20 metres but no more than 50 metres (10 points); 2e: Can stand and then move more than 1 metre but no more than 20 metres, either aided or unaided (12 points); 2f: Cannot, either aided or unaided, –(i) stand; or(ii) move more than 1 metre (12 points)
GIVETH A MAYBE `a level of ability to carry out activities`
DECIDE `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out mobility activities` IS
    CONSIDER `reg 6(3): C's level of ability to carry out mobility activities` `I have undergone an assessment` (`reg 6(1): the score C obtains in mobility activities` `my mobility descriptors`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST level THEN JUST (`reg 4(1): C's level of ability, on the basis of an assessment` level `my limited ability results from my physical or mental condition`)
    WHERE
        `my mobility descriptors` MEANS `the descriptors that apply to C in the mobility activities` WITH
            `for planning and following journeys` IS `my descriptor for planning and following journeys`
            `for moving around` IS `my descriptor for moving around`

-- reg 4(2A), 4(4). I can be assessed as satisfying a descriptor that turns on doing an activity only if I can do it safely, to an
-- acceptable standard, repeatedly and within a reasonable time period.
@export Can I be assessed as satisfying a descriptor that turns on doing an activity (reg 4(2A), 4(4))?
GIVEN `harm to me is likely during or after the activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it likely that doing the activity would cause harm to you, during or after it?
      `harm to another person is likely during or after the activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it likely that doing the activity would cause harm to another person, during or after it?
      `I can do the activity to an acceptable standard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you do the activity to an acceptable standard?
      `the number of times I can complete the activity` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times can you complete the activity?
      `the number of times the activity is reasonably required to be completed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times is the activity reasonably required to be completed?
      `the time I take to complete the activity` IS A NUMBER @desc How long do you take to complete the activity, in minutes?
      `the longest time a person without a limiting condition would normally take` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest time a person without a condition that limits the activity would normally take, in minutes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be assessed as satisfying a descriptor that turns on doing an activity` IF
    `reg 4(2A) and (4): C may be assessed as satisfying a descriptor, from the facts`
        `harm to me is likely during or after the activity`
        `harm to another person is likely during or after the activity`
        `I can do the activity to an acceptable standard`
        `the number of times I can complete the activity`
        `the number of times the activity is reasonably required to be completed`
        `the time I take to complete the activity`
        `the longest time a person without a limiting condition would normally take`

-- reg 4(2). I am assessed as if I were wearing or using any aid or appliance that I normally wear or use, or could
-- reasonably be expected to wear or use.
@export Is an aid or appliance taken into account when I am assessed (reg 4(2))?
GIVEN `I normally wear or use it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you normally wear or use the aid or appliance?
      `I could reasonably be expected to wear or use it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could you reasonably be expected to wear or use the aid or appliance?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an aid or appliance taken into account when I am assessed` IF
    `reg 4(2): C's ability is assessed as if C were wearing or using the aid or appliance` `I normally wear or use it` `I could reasonably be expected to wear or use it`

-- reg 7(3). The required period is 3 months and 9 months either side of the prescribed date.
@export How many days are in my required period (reg 7(3))?
GIVEN `my required period is` IS A `which required period applies to me` @desc Which describes your case? (a claim made after an interval under regulation 15 or 15A; any other claim; a day of your award in the 3 months after such a claim; a day of your award in any other case)
      `my prescribed date` IS A DATE @desc What is your prescribed date? (see the question about the prescribed date)
      `the date I made my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make your claim?
      `the day of my award` IS A DATE @desc For a day of your award, which day is it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days are in my required period` IS
    `reg 7(3): the number of days of the required period` `my required period for this case`
    WHERE
        `my required period for this case` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my required period is`
            WHEN `a claim made after an interval, under regulation 15 or 15A` THEN `reg 7(3)(a)(i): the required period for a claim after an interval under regulation 15 or 15A` `my prescribed date` `the date I made my claim`
            WHEN `any other claim` THEN `reg 7(3)(a)(ii): the required period for any other claim` `my prescribed date`
            WHEN `a day of my award in the 3 months after such a claim` THEN `reg 7(3)(b)(i): the required period for a day of an award in the 3 months after a claim for the purpose of regulation 15 or 15A` `my prescribed date` `the day of my award`
            WHEN `a day of my award in any other case` THEN `reg 7(3)(b)(ii): the required period for a day of an award in any other case` `the day of my award`

-- reg 8(2). One month from the request, or a longer period the Secretary of State considers reasonable.
@export By what day must I give the information or evidence the Secretary of State has asked for (reg 8(2))?
GIVEN `the date of the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the request made?
      `the Secretary of State has allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said you have longer than one month, because they consider that reasonable in your circumstances?
      `the last day the Secretary of State has allowed` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day they have allowed? (ignored if you answered no)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I give the information or evidence` IS
    `reg 8(2): the last day for providing the information or evidence` `the date of the request` `the longer period`
    WHERE
        `the longer period` MEANS IF `the Secretary of State has allowed a longer period` THEN JUST `the last day the Secretary of State has allowed` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 8(2), (3). If I do not give the information or evidence in time and the Secretary of State is not satisfied I had good reason,
-- a negative determination must be made for the component the request related to.
@export Must a negative determination be made against me for not giving the information or evidence in time (reg 8(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the date of the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the request made?
      `the Secretary of State has allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said you have longer than one month, because they consider that reasonable in your circumstances?
      `the last day the Secretary of State has allowed` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day they have allowed? (ignored if you answered no)
      `I gave the information or evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the information or evidence?
      `the day I gave it` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day did you give it? (ignored if you answered no)
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that I had good reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State satisfied that you had good reason for not giving it in time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must a negative determination be made against me for not giving the information or evidence in time` IF
    `reg 8(3): a negative determination must be made in relation to the component to which the failure related`
        (`reg 8(2): C provided the information or evidence in time` (`reg 8(2): the last day for providing the information or evidence` `the date of the request` `the longer period`) `the day I provided it`)
        `the Secretary of State is satisfied that I had good reason`
    WHERE
        `the longer period` MEANS IF `the Secretary of State has allowed a longer period` THEN JUST `the last day the Secretary of State has allowed` ELSE NOTHING
        `the day I provided it` MEANS IF `I gave the information or evidence` THEN JUST `the day I gave it` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 9(2), (3), (4), (5). If I fail without good reason to attend or take part in a consultation with a person approved by the Secretary
-- of State, and I was given 7 days' written notice (or agreed to less), a negative determination must be made.
@export Must a negative determination be made against me for missing a consultation (reg 9(2) to (5))?
GIVEN `the consultation is with a person approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the consultation with a person approved by the Secretary of State?
      `I failed to attend or take part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to attend, or to take part in, the consultation?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that I had good reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State satisfied that you had good reason for the failure?
      `the day the notice was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice of the consultation sent to you?
      `the day of the consultation` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the consultation to take place?
      `the notice was in writing on paper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice in writing on paper?
      `the notice was sent by electronic communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice sent by electronic communication?
      `I had agreed to accept correspondence by electronic communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had you agreed to accept correspondence that way?
      `I agreed to accept a shorter period of notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you agree, in writing or otherwise, to accept a shorter period of notice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must a negative determination be made against me for missing a consultation` IF
    `reg 9(2): a negative determination must be made because C failed to attend or participate`
        `the consultation is with a person approved by the Secretary of State`
        `I failed to attend or take part`
        `the Secretary of State is satisfied that I had good reason`
        (`reg 9(3): regulation 9(2) can apply because the notice requirement is met`
            `the day the notice was sent` `the day of the consultation` `the notice was in writing on paper`
            `the notice was sent by electronic communication` `I had agreed to accept correspondence by electronic communication` `I agreed to accept a shorter period of notice`)

-- reg 10. In deciding whether I had good reason, the Secretary of State must take into account my state of health at the relevant
-- time and the nature of any disability I have; the list is a floor, not a closed list.
@export Must the Secretary of State take this matter into account when deciding whether I had good reason (reg 10)?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `a matter that may bear on good reason` @desc Which matter is it? (your state of health at the relevant time; the nature of any disability you have; any other matter)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Secretary of State take this matter into account` IF
    `reg 10: regulation 10 requires this matter to be taken into account in determining good reason` `the matter`

-- reg 11. Once it is determined that I have limited or severely limited ability, the Secretary of State may determine afresh, for
-- any reason and at any time, whether I continue to have it; doing paid work or voluntary work is not a reason.
@export May the Secretary of State look at my ability afresh for this reason (reg 11)?
GIVEN `it has been determined that I have limited ability or severely limited ability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it already been determined that you have limited or severely limited ability?
      `the reason` IS A `a reason for determining afresh` @desc What is the reason? (you are doing work for payment or in expectation of payment; you are doing voluntary work; any other reason)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Secretary of State look at my ability afresh for this reason` IF
    `reg 11: the Secretary of State may determine afresh whether C continues to have limited or severely limited ability, for this reason` `it has been determined that I have limited ability or severely limited ability` `the reason`

§§ `The required period condition (Part 3)`

-- regs 12 and 13. To meet the required period condition for the standard rate I must be likely to be found to have limited ability
-- (and not severely limited ability) at every time in the 3 months ending with my prescribed date and in the 9 months after it; for
-- the enhanced rate, severely limited ability at every time in both. After a previous award, the look-back is treated as met
-- (regs 15A(4), 15B(4)).
@export Which rate of the daily living component do I meet the required period condition for (regs 12(1), 12(2))?
GIVEN `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months before my prescribed date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it likely that the Secretary of State would determine that you had limited ability to carry out daily living activities at every time in the 3 months ending with your prescribed date?
      `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months after my prescribed date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it likely that the Secretary of State would determine that you had limited ability to carry out daily living activities at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after your prescribed date?
      `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months before my prescribed date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it likely that the Secretary of State would determine that you had severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities at every time in the 3 months ending with your prescribed date?
      `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months after my prescribed date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it likely that the Secretary of State would determine that you had severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after your prescribed date?
      `my previous award means my look-back is treated as met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4) treat your look-back as met because of your previous award? (see the question about that)
GIVETH A `a rate of a component`
DECIDE `Which rate of the daily living component do I meet the required period condition for` IS
    `regs 12 and 13: the rate of the component whose required period condition is met`
        (`reg 12(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the daily living component is met` `my likely determinations` `with` `my previous award means my look-back is treated as met`)
        `and`
        (`reg 12(2): the required period condition for the enhanced rate of the daily living component is met` `my likely determinations` `with` `my previous award means my look-back is treated as met`)
    WHERE
        `my likely determinations` MEANS `the likely determinations across the two windows` WITH
            `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months ending with the prescribed date` IS `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months before my prescribed date`
            `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date` IS `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months after my prescribed date`
            `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months ending with the prescribed date` IS `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months before my prescribed date`
            `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date` IS `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months after my prescribed date`

-- regs 13(1), 13(2): the same for the mobility component.
@export Which rate of the mobility component do I meet the required period condition for (regs 13(1), 13(2))?
GIVEN `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months before my prescribed date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it likely that the Secretary of State would determine that you had limited ability to carry out mobility activities at every time in the 3 months ending with your prescribed date?
      `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months after my prescribed date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it likely that the Secretary of State would determine that you had limited ability to carry out mobility activities at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after your prescribed date?
      `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months before my prescribed date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it likely that the Secretary of State would determine that you had severely limited ability to carry out mobility activities at every time in the 3 months ending with your prescribed date?
      `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months after my prescribed date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it likely that the Secretary of State would determine that you had severely limited ability to carry out mobility activities at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after your prescribed date?
      `my previous award means my look-back is treated as met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4) treat your look-back as met because of your previous award? (see the question about that)
GIVETH A `a rate of a component`
DECIDE `Which rate of the mobility component do I meet the required period condition for` IS
    `regs 12 and 13: the rate of the component whose required period condition is met`
        (`reg 13(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the mobility component is met` `my likely determinations` `with` `my previous award means my look-back is treated as met`)
        `and`
        (`reg 13(2): the required period condition for the enhanced rate of the mobility component is met` `my likely determinations` `with` `my previous award means my look-back is treated as met`)
    WHERE
        `my likely determinations` MEANS `the likely determinations across the two windows` WITH
            `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months ending with the prescribed date` IS `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months before my prescribed date`
            `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date` IS `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months after my prescribed date`
            `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months ending with the prescribed date` IS `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months before my prescribed date`
            `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date` IS `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months after my prescribed date`

-- reg 14. The prescribed date is, for a claim not yet determined, the date of the claim or, if later, the earliest date from which
-- the Secretary of State would likely have found my ability at every time in the previous 3 months; for an award, each day of it.
@export What is my prescribed date (reg 14)?
GIVEN `I have an award of a component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an award of either or both components?
      `the day of my award` IS A DATE @desc If so, for which day of the award do you want the prescribed date? (ignored if you answered no)
      `the date of my claim` IS A DATE @desc For a claim that has not been determined: on what date did you make it? (ignored if you have an award)
      `there is a later date from which the Secretary of State would likely have determined my ability at every time in the previous 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a date from which, had you been assessed at every time in the previous 3 months, it is likely the Secretary of State would have determined that you had limited or, as the case may be, severely limited ability?
      `that earliest date` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the earliest such date? (ignored if you answered no)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is my prescribed date` IS
    IF `I have an award of a component`
    THEN `reg 14(b): the prescribed date on a day of an award` `the day of my award`
    ELSE `reg 14(a): the prescribed date for a claim that has not been determined` `the date of my claim` `the earliest date, if there is one`
    WHERE
        `the earliest date, if there is one` MEANS
            IF `there is a later date from which the Secretary of State would likely have determined my ability at every time in the previous 3 months`
            THEN JUST `that earliest date`
            ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 15(1), 26(2)(b). A new claim after an interval counts if my previous award of personal independence payment or adult
-- disability payment ended not more than 2 years (1 year if I have reached the relevant age) before the claim, was of the
-- same component, and the Secretary of State determines the entitlement results from the same or a resulting condition.
@export Do I have a claim after an interval, under regulation 15 (reg 15(1))?
GIVEN `the benefit paid under my previous award` IS A `the benefit paid under an earlier award` @desc Which benefit was paid under your previous award? (personal independence payment; adult disability payment; child disability payment; Scottish adult disability living allowance; disability living allowance; some other benefit)
      `the day my previous award ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your previous award end?
      `the day I make my new claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your new claim?
      `I have reached the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the relevant age (the age at which section 83 of the Act stops personal independence payment)?
      `my previous award consisted of the same component as my new claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your previous award consist of the same component as the one you are claiming (or would be entitled to if you met the required period condition)?
      `the Secretary of State determines that my entitlement results from the same condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State determine that your entitlement results from substantially the same physical or mental condition or conditions as the previous award, or from a new condition that developed as a result of one of them?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a claim after an interval under regulation 15` IF
    `reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim`
        `the benefit paid under my previous award`
        `the day my previous award ended`
        `the day I make my new claim`
        (`reg 26(2)(b): the number of years in regulation 15(1)(b)` (`reg 26(1): the exceptions of regulation 26(2) apply` `I have reached the relevant age` TRUE))
        `my previous award consisted of the same component as my new claim`
        `the Secretary of State determines that my entitlement results from the same condition`

-- reg 15A(1), 15A(5). A new claim after child disability payment counts if that award ended not more than 2 years before and I am
-- 16 or over on the day of the claim. If I claim within the 13 week period of the Scottish regulations the award is treated as
-- having ended just before the claim.
@export Do I have a claim after child disability payment, under regulation 15A (reg 15A(1), (5))?
GIVEN `the benefit paid under my previous award` IS A `the benefit paid under an earlier award` @desc Which benefit was paid under your previous award? (personal independence payment; adult disability payment; child disability payment; Scottish adult disability living allowance; disability living allowance; some other benefit)
      `the day my previous award ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your previous award end?
      `the day I make my new claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your new claim?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I make my new claim during the 13 week period provided for in regulation 36` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make your new claim during the 13 week period provided for in regulation 36 of the Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a claim after child disability payment under regulation 15A` IF
    `reg 15A(1): regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply to the new claim`
        `the benefit paid under my previous award`
        (`reg 15A(5): the day the previous child disability payment award is treated as having ended` `the day my previous award ended` `the day I make my new claim` `I make my new claim during the 13 week period provided for in regulation 36`)
        `the day I make my new claim`
        `my date of birth`

-- reg 15B(1), 15B(6), 26A(2)(b). A new claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance counts if that award ended not more
-- than 2 years (1 year if I have reached the relevant age) before, I have not been entitled to personal independence payment
-- since, and I was 64 or younger on 8 April 2013.
@export Do I have a claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance, under regulation 15B (reg 15B(1), (6))?
GIVEN `the benefit paid under my previous award` IS A `the benefit paid under an earlier award` @desc Which benefit was paid under your previous award? (personal independence payment; adult disability payment; child disability payment; Scottish adult disability living allowance; disability living allowance; some other benefit)
      `the day my previous award ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your previous award end?
      `the day I make my new claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your new claim?
      `I have reached the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the relevant age (the age at which section 83 of the Act stops personal independence payment)?
      `I have been entitled to personal independence payment on a day since my previous award ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been entitled to personal independence payment on any day since your previous award ended?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I make my new claim during the 13 week period provided for in regulation 48` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make your new claim during the 13 week period provided for in regulation 48 of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance under regulation 15B` IF
    `reg 15B(1): regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply to the new claim`
        `the benefit paid under my previous award`
        (`reg 15B(6): the day the previous Scottish adult disability living allowance award is treated as having ended` `the day my previous award ended` `the day I make my new claim` `I make my new claim during the 13 week period provided for in regulation 48`)
        `the day I make my new claim`
        (`reg 26A(2)(b): the number of years in regulation 15B(1)(b)` (`reg 26A(1): the exceptions of regulation 26A(2) apply` `I have reached the relevant age` TRUE))
        `I have been entitled to personal independence payment on a day since my previous award ended`
        `my date of birth`

-- regs 15A(4), 15B(4). Where regulation 15A or 15B applies to my new claim, I am regarded as meeting the look-back limb of
-- regulations 12 and 13.
@export Does my previous award mean my look-back is treated as met (regs 15A(4), 15B(4))?
GIVEN `regulation 15A applies to my new claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 15A apply to your new claim? (see the question about regulation 15A)
      `regulation 15B applies to my new claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 15B apply to your new claim? (see the question about regulation 15B)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my previous award mean my look-back is treated as met` IF
       `reg 15A(4): limb (a) of regulations 12 and 13 is regarded as met` `regulation 15A applies to my new claim`
    OR `reg 15B(4): limb (a) of regulations 12 and 13 is regarded as met` `regulation 15B applies to my new claim`

-- regs 14 to 15B. Regulation 14 applies except where paragraph (2) or (3) of regulation 15, 15A or 15B applies; (2) is for determining
-- entitlement under the new claim, (3) for the first 3 months of the award that follows.
@export Which regulation sets the dates my required period condition is tested at (regs 14 to 15B)?
GIVEN `regulation 15 applies to my new claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 15 apply to your new claim? (see the question about regulation 15)
      `regulation 15A applies to my new claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 15A apply to your new claim? (see the question about regulation 15A)
      `regulation 15B applies to my new claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 15B apply to your new claim? (see the question about regulation 15B)
      `the stage I am asking about` IS A `the stage at which the prescribed date is wanted` @desc Are you asking about determining entitlement under the new claim, or about continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim?
GIVETH A `the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at`
DECIDE `Which regulation sets the dates my required period condition is tested at` IS
    `regs 14 to 15B: the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` `regulation 15 applies to my new claim` `regulation 15A applies to my new claim` `regulation 15B applies to my new claim` `the stage I am asking about`

-- The two dates from which the windows run, for each of the regulations that can fix them.
GIVEN provision IS A `the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at`
      `the prescribed date under regulation 14` IS A DATE
      `the day the previous award ended` IS A DATE
      `the day the new claim is made` IS A DATE
      `the day of the award` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `the dates the required period condition is tested at`
`seat: the dates the required period condition is tested at` provision `with` `the prescribed date under regulation 14` `and` `the day the previous award ended` `and` `the day the new claim is made` `and` `the day of the award` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `regulation 14, there being no claim after an interval` THEN
        JUST (`the dates the required period condition is tested at` OF `the prescribed date under regulation 14`, `the prescribed date under regulation 14`)
    WHEN `regulation 15(2)` THEN JUST (`reg 15(2): the dates for determining entitlement under the new claim` `the day the previous award ended` `the day the new claim is made`)
    WHEN `regulation 15(3)` THEN JUST (`reg 15(3): the dates for continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` `the day the previous award ended` `the day of the award`)
    WHEN `regulation 15A(2)` THEN JUST (`reg 15A(2): the dates for determining entitlement under the new claim` `the day the previous award ended` `the day the new claim is made`)
    WHEN `regulation 15A(3)` THEN JUST (`reg 15A(3): the dates for entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` `the day the previous award ended` `the day of the award`)
    WHEN `regulation 15B(2)` THEN JUST (`reg 15B(2): the dates for determining entitlement under the new claim` `the day the previous award ended` `the day the new claim is made`)
    WHEN `regulation 15B(3)` THEN JUST (`reg 15B(3): the dates for continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` `the day the previous award ended` `the day of the award`)
    WHEN `more than one of regulations 15, 15A and 15B applies, and the text does not say which prevails` THEN NOTHING

@export From which day does my 3-month look-back run (regs 12 to 15B)?
GIVEN `the regulation that sets my dates` IS A `the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` @desc Which regulation sets the dates for your required period condition? (see the question about that)
      `my prescribed date under regulation 14` IS A DATE @desc What is your prescribed date under regulation 14? (see the question about the prescribed date)
      `the day my previous award ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your previous award end? (ignored if you have none)
      `the day I make my new claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your new claim? (ignored if you have no claim after an interval)
      `the day of my award` IS A DATE @desc For a day of your award, which day is it? (ignored if you are not asking about an award)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which day does my 3-month look-back run` IS
    CONSIDER `seat: the dates the required period condition is tested at` `the regulation that sets my dates` `with` `my prescribed date under regulation 14` `and` `the day my previous award ended` `and` `the day I make my new claim` `and` `the day of my award`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST dates THEN JUST (dates's `the date the 3 months look back from`)

@export After which day do my 9 months run (regs 12 to 15B)?
GIVEN `the regulation that sets my dates` IS A `the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` @desc Which regulation sets the dates for your required period condition? (see the question about that)
      `my prescribed date under regulation 14` IS A DATE @desc What is your prescribed date under regulation 14? (see the question about the prescribed date)
      `the day my previous award ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your previous award end? (ignored if you have none)
      `the day I make my new claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your new claim? (ignored if you have no claim after an interval)
      `the day of my award` IS A DATE @desc For a day of your award, which day is it? (ignored if you are not asking about an award)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `After which day do my 9 months run` IS
    CONSIDER `seat: the dates the required period condition is tested at` `the regulation that sets my dates` `with` `my prescribed date under regulation 14` `and` `the day my previous award ended` `and` `the day I make my new claim` `and` `the day of my award`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST dates THEN JUST (dates's `the date the 9 months look forward from`)

§§ `Residence and presence (Part 4)`

-- reg 16(a), 23ZC(6). I must be present in England and Wales on the day, or treated as present (regs 17 to 19, 20A, 23ZB(2), 23ZC(7)(a)).
-- For the decision on an ongoing claim after a move to Scotland, "Great Britain" is read for "England and Wales" (reg 23ZC(6)).
@export Am I present in England and Wales on this day, or treated as present (reg 16(a))?
GIVEN `I am present in England and Wales on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you present in England and Wales on the day?
      `I am present in Great Britain on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you present in Great Britain on the day?
      `the Secretary of State must decide my ongoing claim under regulation 23ZC(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must the Secretary of State decide your ongoing claim under regulation 23ZC(5), after your move to Scotland? (see the question about regulation 23ZC)
      `regulations 17 to 19 treat me as present on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations 17 to 19 treat you as present on the day, because of an absence from Great Britain? (see the questions about your absence)
      `regulation 20A treats me as present on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 20A treat you as present in England and Wales on the day, because you are present in Scotland? (see the question about regulation 20A)
      `regulation 23ZB(2) or 23ZC(7) treats me as present on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 23ZB(2) or 23ZC(7)(a) treat you as present in England and Wales on the day, in the run-on period after you moved to Scotland? (see the questions about those regulations)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I present in England and Wales on this day, or treated as present` IF
    `reg 16(a): C is present in England and Wales on the day`
        `I am present in England and Wales on the day`
        `I am present in Great Britain on the day`
        (`reg 23ZC(6): regulation 16(a) is read with "Great Britain" in place of "England and Wales" for the decision` `the Secretary of State must decide my ongoing claim under regulation 23ZC(5)`)
        (`reg 16(a): C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day by one of regulations 17 to 19, 20A, 23ZB(2) and 23ZC(7)`
            `regulations 17 to 19 treat me as present on the day` `regulation 20A treats me as present on the day` `regulation 23ZB(2) or 23ZC(7) treats me as present on the day`)

-- regs 17 to 19. While I am temporarily absent from Great Britain I am treated as present for the first 13 weeks (regulation 17), the
-- first 26 weeks if the absence is for medical treatment (regulation 18) or after the Government advised nationals to leave a
-- country or evacuated them (regulations 18A, 18C), up to 26 weeks in all (regulations 18B, 18D); and without limit in the special
-- cases of regulation 19.
@export Am I treated as present on this day of my absence from Great Britain (regs 17 to 19)?
GIVEN `the weeks of my absence as at the day` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks into your absence from Great Britain is the day? (13 weeks in, give 13)
      `at the beginning of my absence, it was unlikely to exceed 52 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the beginning of your absence from Great Britain, was it unlikely to last more than 52 weeks?
      `my absence is solely for arranged medical treatment of a condition that began before I left` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your absence solely in connection with arrangements made for your medical treatment for a disease or bodily or mental disablement which began before you left Great Britain?
      `the arrangements relate to medical treatment outside Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the arrangements relate to medical treatment outside Great Britain?
      `the arrangements relate to medical treatment during my temporary absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the arrangements relate to medical treatment during the period you are temporarily absent from Great Britain?
      `the treatment is by or under the supervision of a person appropriately qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the treatment by, or under the supervision of, a person appropriately qualified to carry it out?
      `I was in a country outside Great Britain when the Government gave public information to leave it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it?
      `I was in a country outside Great Britain when the Government arranged an evacuation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect me to return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect you to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain?
      `the Scottish Ministers are satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect me to return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the Scottish Ministers satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect you to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain?
      `I did not enter that country when the Government's public information was to leave it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that you did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty's Government's public information was to advise British nationals to leave it?
      `regulation 19(1) applies to my absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 19(1) treat you as present because of your capacity or circumstances while abroad? (see the question about regulation 19)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as present on this day of my absence` IF
    `regs 17 to 19: C is treated as present on the day of this absence` `my absence` `as at` `the weeks of my absence as at the day`
    WHERE
        `my absence` MEANS `an absence from Great Britain` WITH
            `at the beginning of the absence, the absence was unlikely to exceed 52 weeks` IS `at the beginning of my absence, it was unlikely to exceed 52 weeks`
            `the absence is solely in connection with arrangements made for the medical treatment of C for a disease or bodily or mental disablement which commenced before C left Great Britain` IS `my absence is solely for arranged medical treatment of a condition that began before I left`
            `the arrangements relate to medical treatment outside Great Britain` IS `the arrangements relate to medical treatment outside Great Britain`
            `the arrangements relate to medical treatment during the period whilst C is temporarily absent from Great Britain` IS `the arrangements relate to medical treatment during my temporary absence`
            `the treatment is by, or under the supervision of, a person appropriately qualified to carry it out` IS `the treatment is by or under the supervision of a person appropriately qualified`
            `C was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it` IS `I was in a country outside Great Britain when the Government gave public information to leave it`
            `C was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it` IS `I was in a country outside Great Britain when the Government arranged an evacuation`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect C to return, or have returned, to Great Britain` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect me to return`
            `the Scottish Ministers are satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect C to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain` IS `the Scottish Ministers are satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect me to return`
            `C did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty's Government's public information was to advise British nationals to leave it` IS `I did not enter that country when the Government's public information was to leave it`
            `regulation 19(1) applies to the absence` IS `regulation 19(1) applies to my absence`
            -- Placeholder: the day rule does not read this field.
            `the weeks of the absence that fall within the 156 weeks` IS 0

@export How many weeks of my absence count as weeks I was present in Great Britain (regs 17 to 19)?
GIVEN `the weeks of my absence that fall within the 156 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of this absence fall within the 156 weeks before the day?
      `at the beginning of my absence, it was unlikely to exceed 52 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the beginning of your absence from Great Britain, was it unlikely to last more than 52 weeks?
      `my absence is solely for arranged medical treatment of a condition that began before I left` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your absence solely in connection with arrangements made for your medical treatment for a disease or bodily or mental disablement which began before you left Great Britain?
      `the arrangements relate to medical treatment outside Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the arrangements relate to medical treatment outside Great Britain?
      `the arrangements relate to medical treatment during my temporary absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the arrangements relate to medical treatment during the period you are temporarily absent from Great Britain?
      `the treatment is by or under the supervision of a person appropriately qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the treatment by, or under the supervision of, a person appropriately qualified to carry it out?
      `I was in a country outside Great Britain when the Government gave public information to leave it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it?
      `I was in a country outside Great Britain when the Government arranged an evacuation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect me to return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect you to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain?
      `the Scottish Ministers are satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect me to return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the Scottish Ministers satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect you to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain?
      `I did not enter that country when the Government's public information was to leave it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that you did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty's Government's public information was to advise British nationals to leave it?
      `regulation 19(1) applies to my absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 19(1) treat you as present because of your capacity or circumstances while abroad? (see the question about regulation 19)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of my absence count as weeks I was present in Great Britain` IS
    `regs 17 to 19: the weeks of this absence treated as present` `my absence`
    WHERE
        `my absence` MEANS `an absence from Great Britain` WITH
            `at the beginning of the absence, the absence was unlikely to exceed 52 weeks` IS `at the beginning of my absence, it was unlikely to exceed 52 weeks`
            `the absence is solely in connection with arrangements made for the medical treatment of C for a disease or bodily or mental disablement which commenced before C left Great Britain` IS `my absence is solely for arranged medical treatment of a condition that began before I left`
            `the arrangements relate to medical treatment outside Great Britain` IS `the arrangements relate to medical treatment outside Great Britain`
            `the arrangements relate to medical treatment during the period whilst C is temporarily absent from Great Britain` IS `the arrangements relate to medical treatment during my temporary absence`
            `the treatment is by, or under the supervision of, a person appropriately qualified to carry it out` IS `the treatment is by or under the supervision of a person appropriately qualified`
            `C was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it` IS `I was in a country outside Great Britain when the Government gave public information to leave it`
            `C was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it` IS `I was in a country outside Great Britain when the Government arranged an evacuation`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect C to return, or have returned, to Great Britain` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect me to return`
            `the Scottish Ministers are satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect C to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain` IS `the Scottish Ministers are satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect me to return`
            `C did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty's Government's public information was to advise British nationals to leave it` IS `I did not enter that country when the Government's public information was to leave it`
            `regulation 19(1) applies to the absence` IS `regulation 19(1) applies to my absence`
            `the weeks of the absence that fall within the 156 weeks` IS `the weeks of my absence that fall within the 156 weeks`

-- reg 16(b). I must have been present in Great Britain for 104 weeks out of the 156 weeks immediately before the day; weeks treated
-- as present count.
@export Have I been present in Great Britain for 104 of the last 156 weeks (reg 16(b))?
GIVEN `the weeks I was present in Great Britain out of the 156 weeks before the day` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many of the 156 weeks immediately before the day were you present in Great Britain? (do not count weeks of absence)
      `the weeks I am treated as present out of those 156 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many of those weeks are you treated as present under regulations 17 to 19? (add up the answers for each absence; see the question about the weeks of an absence)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I been present in Great Britain for 104 of the last 156 weeks` IF
    `reg 16(b): C has been present in Great Britain for not less than 104 weeks out of the 156 weeks` `the weeks I was present in Great Britain out of the 156 weeks before the day` `the weeks I am treated as present out of those 156 weeks`

-- reg 16(c) as modified by regs 20, 23, 23A(1A) and 23ZA.
@export Am I habitually resident in a place that satisfies regulation 16(c), counting regulations 20, 23, 23A(1A) and 23ZA?
GIVEN `my component` IS A `a component of personal independence payment` @desc Which component are you asking about?
      `where I am habitually resident` IS A `a place of habitual residence` @desc Where are you habitually resident? (the United Kingdom; the Republic of Ireland; the Isle of Man; the Channel Islands; an EEA state other than the Republic of Ireland; Switzerland; some other place)
      `regulation 20 treats me as habitually resident in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 20 treat you as habitually resident in Great Britain? (see the question about regulation 20)
      `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c) for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 23 mean regulation 16(a) to (c) do not apply to you? (see the question about regulation 23)
      `regulation 23A(1A) disapplies regulation 16(c) for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 23A mean regulation 16(c) does not apply to you? (see the question about regulation 23A)
      `regulation 23ZA treats regulation 16(c) as not satisfied for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 23ZA treat regulation 16(c) as not satisfied for you on the day? (see the question about regulation 23ZA)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I habitually resident in a place that satisfies regulation 16(c)` IS
    `reg 16(c) as modified: limb (c) is met` `my component` `with` `regulation 20 treats me as habitually resident in Great Britain` `and` `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c) for me` `and` `regulation 23A(1A) disapplies regulation 16(c) for me` `and` `regulation 23ZA treats regulation 16(c) as not satisfied for me` `and`
        (`reg 16(c): C is habitually resident in the United Kingdom, the Republic of Ireland, the Isle of Man or the Channel Islands` `where I am habitually resident`)

-- reg 16(d).
@export Am I a person who is not excluded by immigration control (reg 16(d))?
GIVEN `I am not subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999?
      `section 115 of that Act does not apply to me for the purpose of personal independence payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 115 of that Act not apply to you for the purpose of personal independence payment, by virtue of regulation 2 of the Social Security (Immigration and Asylum) Consequential Amendments Regulations 2000?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a person who is not excluded by immigration control` IF
    `reg 16(d): C is a person who is not excluded by immigration control` `I am not subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999` `section 115 of that Act does not apply to me for the purpose of personal independence payment`

-- reg 16 as a whole, with regs 21, 22, 23, 23A and 23ZA.
@export Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day?
GIVEN `my component` IS A `a component of personal independence payment` @desc Which component are you asking about?
      `limb (a) is met on its own terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you present in England and Wales on the day, or treated as present? (see the question about regulation 16(a))
      `limb (b) is met on its own terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been present in Great Britain for 104 of the last 156 weeks? (see the question about regulation 16(b))
      `where I am habitually resident` IS A `a place of habitual residence` @desc Where are you habitually resident? (the United Kingdom; the Republic of Ireland; the Isle of Man; the Channel Islands; an EEA state other than the Republic of Ireland; Switzerland; some other place)
      `I am not subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999?
      `section 115 of that Act does not apply to me for the purpose of personal independence payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 115 of that Act not apply to you for the purpose of personal independence payment, by virtue of regulation 2 of the 2000 Regulations?
      `regulation 20 treats me as habitually resident in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 20 treat you as habitually resident in Great Britain? (see the question about regulation 20)
      `regulation 21 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 21 apply to you, because you are terminally ill and claim expressly on that ground? (see the question about regulation 21)
      `regulation 22 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 22 apply to you? (see the question about regulation 22)
      `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c) for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 23 mean regulation 16(a) to (c) do not apply to you? (see the question about regulation 23)
      `regulation 23A applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 23A mean regulation 16(b) and (c) do not apply to you? (see the question about regulation 23A)
      `regulation 23ZA treats regulation 16(c) as not satisfied for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 23ZA treat regulation 16(c) as not satisfied for you on the day? (see the question about regulation 23ZA)
GIVETH A `the outcome of regulation 16 on the day`
DECIDE `Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day` IS
    `reg 16: the outcome on the day`
        (`reg 16(a) as modified: limb (a) is met` `my component` `with` `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c) for me` `and` `limb (a) is met on its own terms`)
        (`reg 16(b) as modified: limb (b) is met` `my component` `with` `regulation 21 applies to me` `and` `regulation 22 applies to me` `and` `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c) for me` `and` `regulation 23A applies to me` `and` `limb (b) is met on its own terms`)
        (`reg 16(c) as modified: limb (c) is met` `my component` `with` `regulation 20 treats me as habitually resident in Great Britain` `and` `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c) for me` `and` `regulation 23A applies to me` `and` `regulation 23ZA treats regulation 16(c) as not satisfied for me` `and`
            (`reg 16(c): C is habitually resident in the United Kingdom, the Republic of Ireland, the Isle of Man or the Channel Islands` `where I am habitually resident`))
        (`reg 16(d): C is a person who is not excluded by immigration control` `I am not subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999` `section 115 of that Act does not apply to me for the purpose of personal independence payment`)

-- reg 19(2). A member of Her Majesty's forces is a member of the regular or reserve forces (Armed Forces Act 2006 s 374) who is not
-- specified in Schedule 2, is over 16, and is not absent on desertion.
@export Am I a member of Her Majesty's forces for regulations 19 and 20 (reg 19(2), Schedule 2)?
GIVEN `I am a member of the regular forces or the reserve forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the regular forces or the reserve forces, as defined in section 374 of the Armed Forces Act 2006?
      `I am specified in Schedule 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you specified in Schedule 2 to the Regulations? (see the question about Schedule 2)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking?
      `I am absent on desertion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you absent on desertion?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a member of Her Majesty's forces for regulations 19 and 20` IF
    `reg 19(2): the person is a member of Her Majesty's forces on the day` `I am a member of the regular forces or the reserve forces` `I am specified in Schedule 2` `my date of birth` `the day` `I am absent on desertion`

-- Schedule 2. A person who is in the forces is outside regulation 19(2) if they are a locally entered naval person, a military
-- person recruited abroad, or an air force person recruited abroad.
@export Am I specified in Schedule 2, so that I am not a member of Her Majesty's forces (Schedule 2, paragraph 1)?
GIVEN `I am serving in a naval force of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you serving as a member of a naval force of Her Majesty's forces?
      `I locally entered that force at a naval base outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you locally enter that force at a naval base outside the United Kingdom?
      `I have previously been an insured person under Part 1 of the National Insurance Act 1965` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you previously been an insured person under Part 1 of the National Insurance Act 1965?
      `I am paying or have paid primary Class 1 contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paying, or have you previously paid, primary Class 1 contributions?
      `I am paying or have paid Class 2 contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paying, or have you previously paid, Class 2 contributions?
      `I am paying or have paid Class 3 contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paying, or have you previously paid, Class 3 contributions?
      `I am serving in a military force of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you serving as a member of a military force of Her Majesty's forces?
      `I entered that military force or was recruited for it outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you enter that force, or were you recruited for it, outside the United Kingdom?
      `the depot of my unit is outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the depot of your unit outside the United Kingdom?
      `I am serving in an air force of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you serving as a member of an air force of Her Majesty's forces?
      `I entered that air force or was recruited for it outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you enter that air force, or were you recruited for it, outside the United Kingdom?
      `I am liable under my terms of engagement to serve only in a specified part of the world outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you liable under your terms of engagement to serve only in a specified part of the world outside the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I specified in Schedule 2` IF
    `Sch 2 para 1: the person is specified in Schedule 2`
        (`Sch 2 para 1(a): the person is not a member of Her Majesty's forces as a locally entered naval person` `I am serving in a naval force of Her Majesty's forces` `I locally entered that force at a naval base outside the United Kingdom` (`Sch 2 para 2: paragraph 1(a) does not include the person` `I have previously been an insured person under Part 1 of the National Insurance Act 1965` `I am paying or have paid primary Class 1 contributions` `I am paying or have paid Class 2 contributions` `I am paying or have paid Class 3 contributions`))
        (`Sch 2 para 1(b): the person is not a member of Her Majesty's forces as a military person recruited abroad` `I am serving in a military force of Her Majesty's forces` `I entered that military force or was recruited for it outside the United Kingdom` `the depot of my unit is outside the United Kingdom`)
        (`Sch 2 para 1(c): the person is not a member of Her Majesty's forces as an air force person recruited abroad` `I am serving in an air force of Her Majesty's forces` `I entered that air force or was recruited for it outside the United Kingdom` `I am liable under my terms of engagement to serve only in a specified part of the world outside the United Kingdom`)

-- reg 19(3), "aircraft worker". Employed under a contract of service as a pilot, commander, navigator or other crew member, or in
-- another capacity on board an aircraft for the aircraft's purposes under a contract made in the United Kingdom for performance
-- in flight; but not a member of Her Majesty's forces.
@export Am I an aircraft worker (reg 19(3))?
GIVEN `I am employed under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed under a contract of service?
      `I am employed as a pilot, commander, navigator or other member of the crew of an aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed as a pilot, commander, navigator or other member of the crew of an aircraft?
      `I am employed on board an aircraft in another capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in any other capacity on board an aircraft?
      `that employment is for the purposes of the aircraft, its crew, or its passengers, cargo or mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that employment for the purposes of the aircraft or its crew or of any passengers or cargo or mail carried on it?
      `my contract was entered into in the United Kingdom for performance while the aircraft is in flight` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your contract entered into in the United Kingdom with a view to its performance (in whole or in part) while the aircraft is in flight?
      `I am in employment as a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in employment as a member of Her Majesty's forces?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an aircraft worker` IF
    `reg 19(3): the person is an aircraft worker`
        `I am employed under a contract of service`
        `I am employed as a pilot, commander, navigator or other member of the crew of an aircraft`
        (`reg 19(3) "aircraft worker": the other-capacity limb is met` `I am employed on board an aircraft in another capacity` `that employment is for the purposes of the aircraft, its crew, or its passengers, cargo or mail` `my contract was entered into in the United Kingdom for performance while the aircraft is in flight`)
        `I am in employment as a member of Her Majesty's forces`

-- reg 19(3), "mariner".
@export Am I a mariner (reg 19(3))?
GIVEN `I am employed under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed under a contract of service?
      `I am employed as a master or member of the crew of a ship or vessel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed as a master or member of the crew of a ship or vessel?
      `I am employed on board a ship or vessel in another capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in any other capacity on board a ship or vessel?
      `that employment is for the purposes of the ship or vessel, its crew, or its passengers, cargo or mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that employment for the purposes of the ship or vessel or the crew or any passengers or cargo or mail carried by it?
      `my contract was entered into in the United Kingdom for performance while the ship or vessel is on voyage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your contract entered into in the United Kingdom with a view to its performance (in whole or in part) while the ship or vessel is on voyage?
      `I am in employment as a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in employment as a member of Her Majesty's forces?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a mariner` IF
    `reg 19(3): the person is a mariner`
        `I am employed under a contract of service`
        `I am employed as a master or member of the crew of a ship or vessel`
        (`reg 19(3) "mariner": the other-capacity limb is met` `I am employed on board a ship or vessel in another capacity` `that employment is for the purposes of the ship or vessel, its crew, or its passengers, cargo or mail` `my contract was entered into in the United Kingdom for performance while the ship or vessel is on voyage`)
        `I am in employment as a member of Her Majesty's forces`

-- reg 19(1). While I am absent from Great Britain, I am treated as present in the relevant area if I am abroad as a member of Her
-- Majesty's forces, an aircraft worker or a mariner, or in prescribed continental shelf employment, or living with a member of the
-- forces to whom I am related in one of the listed ways.
@export Am I treated as present because of my work abroad or a family member's service (reg 19(1))?
GIVEN `I am absent from Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you absent from Great Britain?
      `I am abroad as a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you abroad in the capacity of a member of Her Majesty's forces? (see the question about the forces)
      `I am abroad as an aircraft worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you abroad in the capacity of an aircraft worker? (see the question about aircraft workers)
      `I am abroad as a mariner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you abroad in the capacity of a mariner? (see the question about mariners)
      `I am in prescribed continental shelf employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in employment prescribed for the purposes of section 120 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 in connection with continental shelf operations?
      `I am living with a person who is abroad as a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you living with a person who is abroad in the capacity of a member of Her Majesty's forces?
      `my relationship to that person` IS A `a relationship to a member of Her Majesty's forces` @desc What is your relationship to that person? (spouse; civil partner; son; daughter; step-son; step-daughter; father; father-in-law; step-father; mother; mother-in-law; step-mother; some other relationship)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as present because of my work abroad or a family member's service` IF
    `reg 19(1): C is treated as present in the relevant area` `I am absent from Great Britain`
        (`reg 19(1): one of the circumstances of paragraphs (a) to (c) applies`
            `I am abroad as a member of Her Majesty's forces` `I am abroad as an aircraft worker` `I am abroad as a mariner`
            `I am in prescribed continental shelf employment` `I am living with a person who is abroad as a member of Her Majesty's forces` `my relationship to that person`)

-- reg 20. Where regulation 16(c) asks about habitual residence, I am treated as habitually resident in Great Britain if I am resident
-- outside Great Britain as a member of Her Majesty's forces, or living with such a person to whom I am related in a listed way.
@export Am I treated as habitually resident in Great Britain because of forces service (reg 20)?
GIVEN `I am resident outside Great Britain as a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident outside Great Britain in the capacity of a member of Her Majesty's forces?
      `I am living with a person who is resident outside Great Britain as a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you living with a person who is resident outside Great Britain in the capacity of a member of Her Majesty's forces?
      `my relationship to that person` IS A `a relationship to a member of Her Majesty's forces` @desc What is your relationship to that person? (spouse; civil partner; son; daughter; step-son; step-daughter; father; father-in-law; step-father; mother; mother-in-law; step-mother; some other relationship)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as habitually resident in Great Britain because of forces service` IF
    `reg 20: C is treated as habitually resident in Great Britain for the purposes of regulation 16(c)` `I am resident outside Great Britain as a member of Her Majesty's forces` `I am living with a person who is resident outside Great Britain as a member of Her Majesty's forces` `my relationship to that person`

-- reg 20A. If I am required to be present in England and Wales, and I am absent from it on a day only because I am temporarily absent
-- from England and Wales, and I am present in Scotland, I am treated as present in England and Wales.
@export Am I treated as present in England and Wales while I am in Scotland (reg 20A)?
GIVEN `I am required to be present in England and Wales for regulation 16(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required, for regulation 16(a), to be present in England and Wales?
      `I am absent from England and Wales on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you absent from England and Wales on the day?
      `my absence on that day is by reason only of a temporary absence from England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your absence on that day by reason only of the fact that you are temporarily absent from England and Wales?
      `I am present in Scotland on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you present in Scotland on the day?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as present in England and Wales while I am in Scotland` IF
    `reg 20A: C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day` `I am required to be present in England and Wales for regulation 16(a)` `I am absent from England and Wales on the day` `my absence on that day is by reason only of a temporary absence from England and Wales` `I am present in Scotland on the day`

-- reg 21. A claim made expressly on the ground that I am terminally ill is exempt from the 104-in-156-weeks test (regulation 16(b)).
@export Is the 104-week presence test (regulation 16(b)) set aside because I am terminally ill (reg 21)?
GIVEN `I am terminally ill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you terminally ill (within the meaning of section 82 of the Act)?
      `I make my claim expressly on the ground that I am terminally ill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make your claim for personal independence payment expressly on the ground that you are terminally ill?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the 104-week presence test set aside because I am terminally ill` IF
    `reg 21: regulation 16 applies as if paragraph (b) were omitted` `I am terminally ill` `I make my claim expressly on the ground that I am terminally ill`

-- reg 22. Regulation 16(b) does not apply on a day when I am habitually resident in Great Britain, a relevant EU Regulation applies, and
-- I can demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom.
@export Is the 104-week presence test set aside because a relevant EU Regulation applies to me in Great Britain (reg 22)?
GIVEN `I am habitually resident in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you habitually resident in Great Britain?
      `a relevant EU Regulation applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a relevant EU Regulation (as defined in the Regulations) apply to you?
      `I can demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the 104-week presence test set aside because a relevant EU Regulation applies to me in Great Britain` IF
    `reg 22: regulation 16(b) does not apply on the day` `I am habitually resident in Great Britain` `a relevant EU Regulation applies to me` `I can demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom`

-- reg 23. For the daily living component, regulation 16(a) to (c) do not apply on a day when I am habitually resident in an EEA state
-- or Switzerland, a relevant EU Regulation applies (or applied on 31 December 2020 and I have been in continuous receipt since, unless
-- I have been habitually resident in the United Kingdom after that date), and I can demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link.
@export Are the presence and residence tests (regulation 16(a) to (c)) set aside for my daily living component because I live in an EEA state or Switzerland (reg 23)?
GIVEN `where I am habitually resident` IS A `a place of habitual residence` @desc Where are you habitually resident? (the United Kingdom; the Republic of Ireland; the Isle of Man; the Channel Islands; an EEA state other than the Republic of Ireland; Switzerland; some other place)
      `a relevant EU Regulation applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a relevant EU Regulation (as defined in the Regulations) apply to you on the day?
      `a relevant EU Regulation applied to me on 31 December 2020` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a relevant EU Regulation apply to you on 31 December 2020?
      `I have been habitually resident in the United Kingdom on a day after 31 December 2020` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been habitually resident in the United Kingdom on any day after 31 December 2020?
      `the latest day I was habitually resident in the United Kingdom` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the latest day you were habitually resident in the United Kingdom? (ignored if you answered no)
      `I have been in continuous receipt of the daily living component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been in continuous receipt of the daily living component up to the day?
      `the first day of my continuous receipt` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day did your continuous receipt begin? (ignored if you answered no)
      `I can demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the presence and residence tests set aside for my daily living component because I live in an EEA state or Switzerland` IF
    `reg 23: regulation 16(a) to (c) do not apply to the daily living component on the day`
        (`reg 23(a): C is habitually resident in an EEA state or Switzerland` `where I am habitually resident`)
        (`reg 23(b): a relevant EU Regulation applies to C, or applied to C on 31 December 2020 and C has been in continuous receipt` `a relevant EU Regulation applies to me` `a relevant EU Regulation applied to me on 31 December 2020` `the latest day, if any` `the first day, if any`)
        `I can demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom`
    WHERE
        `the latest day, if any` MEANS IF `I have been habitually resident in the United Kingdom on a day after 31 December 2020` THEN JUST `the latest day I was habitually resident in the United Kingdom` ELSE NOTHING
        `the first day, if any` MEANS IF `I have been in continuous receipt of the daily living component` THEN JUST `the first day of my continuous receipt` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 23ZA. If I was in receipt of child disability payment or adult disability payment and move to England or Wales within the
-- 13 week period of the Scottish regulations, regulation 16(c) is treated as not satisfied for that period.
@export Is regulation 16(c) treated as not satisfied for me because I moved from Scotland (reg 23ZA)?
GIVEN `regulation 36(1) of the 2021 Scottish Regulations applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 36(1) of the Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021 apply to you?
      `the day is within the period set out in regulation 36(1) of those Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day within the period set out in regulation 36(1) of those Regulations?
      `regulation 53(1) of the 2022 Scottish Regulations applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 53(1) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 apply to you?
      `the day is within the period set out in regulation 53(1) of those Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day within the period set out in regulation 53(1) of those Regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is regulation 16(c) treated as not satisfied for me because I moved from Scotland` IF
    `reg 23ZA: regulation 16(c) is treated as not satisfied on the day by paragraph (1) or (2)`
        (`reg 23ZA(1): regulation 16(c) is treated as not satisfied on the day` `regulation 36(1) of the 2021 Scottish Regulations applies to me` `the day is within the period set out in regulation 36(1) of those Regulations`)
        (`reg 23ZA(2): regulation 16(c) is treated as not satisfied on the day` `regulation 53(1) of the 2022 Scottish Regulations applies to me` `the day is within the period set out in regulation 53(1) of those Regulations`)

-- reg 23ZB(2), (4). If I am entitled to a component on the day before I become permanently resident in Scotland, I am treated as
-- present in England and Wales for the 13 weeks beginning on that date (this regulation applies where that date is 6 November 2025 or later).
@export Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after I move to Scotland (reg 23ZB(2), (4))?
GIVEN `the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you become permanently resident in Scotland?
      `I am entitled to a component on the day before that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a component of personal independence payment on the day before that date?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after I move to Scotland` IF
    `reg 23ZB(2): C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day` `the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` `with` `I am entitled to a component on the day before that date` `on` `the day`

-- reg 23ZB(3). A fixed term award due to expire before the end of the run-on period is extended to the end of the run-on period.
@export On what day does my fixed term award end after the extension (reg 23ZB(3))?
GIVEN `the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you become permanently resident in Scotland?
      `I have an award of a component for a fixed term on the day before that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an award of a component for a fixed term period on the day before that date?
      `the last day of my fixed term` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that fixed term period?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my fixed term award end after the extension` IS
    `reg 23ZB(3): the last day of the fixed term period after any extension` `the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` `I have an award of a component for a fixed term on the day before that date` `the last day of my fixed term`

-- reg 23ZC(3). My claim is ongoing on the date I become permanently resident in Scotland unless, before that date, it was decided,
-- withdrawn, or otherwise ceased to be under consideration.
@export Is my claim still ongoing on the date I become permanently resident in Scotland (reg 23ZC(3))?
GIVEN `my claim was decided under section 8 of the 1998 Act before that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your claim decided by the Secretary of State under section 8 of the Social Security Act 1998 before that date?
      `I withdrew my claim before that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you withdraw your claim in accordance with regulation 31 of the Claims and Payments Regulations before that date?
      `my claim otherwise ceased to be under consideration before that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your claim otherwise cease to be under consideration, before being decided, before that date?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim still ongoing on the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` IF
    `reg 23ZC(3): C has an ongoing claim on the residence change date` `my claim was decided under section 8 of the 1998 Act before that date` `I withdrew my claim before that date` `my claim otherwise ceased to be under consideration before that date`

-- reg 23ZC(2)(c), (4). Present in England and Wales, or treated as present by another provision; for a day before 6 November 2025,
-- present in England and Wales or treated as present in Great Britain.
@export Am I present or treated as present on this day for the purposes of regulation 23ZC (reg 23ZC(2)(c), (4))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking?
      `I am present in England and Wales on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you present in England and Wales on the day?
      `another provision treats me as present in England and Wales on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision other than regulation 23ZC treat you, for regulation 16(a), as present in England and Wales on the day?
      `I am treated as present in Great Britain on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated, for regulation 16(a), as present in Great Britain on the day?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I present or treated as present on this day for the purposes of regulation 23ZC` IF
    `reg 23ZC(2)(c) and (4): C is present or treated as present on the day` `the day` `I am present in England and Wales on the day` `another provision treats me as present in England and Wales on the day` `I am treated as present in Great Britain on the day`

-- reg 23ZC(1), (2), (5). If my claim is ongoing when I become permanently resident in Scotland, and I am present (or treated as present)
-- on the day I claimed and the day before, the Secretary of State must decide it, unless I withdraw it.
@export Must the Secretary of State decide my claim under section 8 of the 1998 Act after my move to Scotland (reg 23ZC(1), (5))?
GIVEN `my claim is ongoing on the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim ongoing on that date? (see the question about regulation 23ZC(3))
      `the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you become permanently resident in Scotland?
      `I was present or treated as present on the day I made my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you present in England and Wales, or treated as present, on the day you made your claim? (see the previous question)
      `I was present or treated as present on the day before that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you present in England and Wales, or treated as present, on the day before that date?
      `I withdraw my claim under regulation 31` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you withdraw your claim in accordance with regulation 31 of the Claims and Payments Regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Secretary of State decide my claim under section 8 of the 1998 Act after my move to Scotland` IF
    `reg 23ZC(1) and (5): the Secretary of State must decide C's claim under section 8 of the 1998 Act`
        (`reg 23ZC(2): C satisfies the conditions` `my claim is ongoing on the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` `the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` `I was present or treated as present on the day I made my claim` `I was present or treated as present on the day before that date`)
        `I withdraw my claim under regulation 31`

-- reg 23ZC(7)(a). If the Secretary of State decides I am entitled, I am treated as present in England and Wales during the run-on period.
@export Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after my move, because my ongoing claim is decided (reg 23ZC(7)(a))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State must decide my claim under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must the Secretary of State decide your claim under regulation 23ZC(5)? (see the previous question)
      `the Secretary of State decides that I am entitled to a component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State decide that you are entitled to a component of personal independence payment?
      `the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you become permanently resident in Scotland?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after my move because my ongoing claim is decided` IF
    `reg 23ZC(7)(a): C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day` `the Secretary of State must decide my claim under paragraph (5)` `the Secretary of State decides that I am entitled to a component` `the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` `the day`

-- reg 23ZC(7)(b). A fixed term award made on that decision that would expire before the end of the run-on period is extended.
@export On what day does my fixed term award end after the extension on a decision of my ongoing claim (reg 23ZC(7)(b))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State must decide my claim under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must the Secretary of State decide your claim under regulation 23ZC(5)? (see the question about that)
      `the Secretary of State decides that I am entitled to a component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State decide that you are entitled to a component of personal independence payment?
      `the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you become permanently resident in Scotland?
      `my award is for a fixed term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your award of a component for a fixed term period?
      `the last day of my fixed term` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that fixed term period?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my fixed term award end after the extension on a decision of my ongoing claim` IS
    `reg 23ZC(7)(b): the last day of the fixed term period after any extension` `the Secretary of State must decide my claim under paragraph (5)` `the Secretary of State decides that I am entitled to a component` `the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` `my award is for a fixed term` `the last day of my fixed term`

-- reg 23A(1), (1A), (1B), (1C). Regulation 16(b) (and 16(c)) do not apply to a claim where I have one of the listed statuses: refugee
-- status or humanitarian protection, leave as a dependant, Afghan schemes, leave from certain countries in crisis (Ukraine, Sudan, Israel
-- and the region), leave following a Government advice to leave a country or an evacuation, or leave on a humanitarian route.
@export Do regulation 16(b) and (c) not apply to me because of my status (reg 23A(1), (1A))?
GIVEN `I have been granted refugee status or humanitarian protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been granted refugee status or humanitarian protection under the immigration rules?
      `I have leave as the dependant of a person granted refugee status or humanitarian protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom as the dependant of a person granted refugee status or humanitarian protection under the immigration rules?
      `I have leave under the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under the immigration rules by virtue of the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy?
      `I have leave under the previous scheme for locally-employed staff in Afghanistan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under the immigration rules by virtue of the previous scheme for locally-employed staff in Afghanistan?
      `I have discretionary leave as the dependant of a person with leave under the Afghan schemes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been granted discretionary leave outside the immigration rules as a dependant of a person who has leave under the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy or the previous scheme?
      `I have leave under the Afghan Citizens Resettlement Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have leave granted under the Afghan Citizens Resettlement Scheme?
      `I have leave granted under or outside the immigration rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under or outside the immigration rules?
      `I have a right of abode` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971?
      `I do not require leave under section 3ZA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of the Immigration Act 1971?
      `I was residing in Ukraine immediately before 1 January 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you residing in Ukraine immediately before 1 January 2022?
      `I left Ukraine in connection with the Russian invasion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you leave Ukraine in connection with the Russian invasion which took place on 24 February 2022?
      `I was residing in Sudan before 15 April 2023` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you residing in Sudan before 15 April 2023?
      `I left Sudan in connection with the violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you leave Sudan in connection with the violence which rapidly escalated on 15 April 2023 in Khartoum and across Sudan?
      `I was residing in Israel or the region immediately before 7 October 2023` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you residing in Israel, the West Bank, the Gaza Strip, East Jerusalem, the Golan Heights or Lebanon immediately before 7 October 2023?
      `I left Israel or the region in connection with the attack or the violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you leave Israel, the West Bank, the Gaza Strip, East Jerusalem, the Golan Heights or Lebanon in connection with the Hamas terrorist attack in Israel on 7 October 2023 or the violence which rapidly escalated in the region following it?
      `I was residing outside Great Britain when the Government advised British nationals to leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you residing in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it?
      `I was residing outside Great Britain when the Government arranged the evacuation of British nationals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you residing in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it?
      `I have left that country or territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you left that country or territory?
      `the day the public information was issued or the evacuation started` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the public information issued, or the evacuation started?
      `the day I arrived in Great Britain` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you arrive in Great Britain?
      `I have leave under the immigration rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with the immigration rules?
      `I have leave on a discretionary basis outside the immigration rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have leave on a discretionary basis outside the immigration rules?
      `I have leave as part of a safe and legal humanitarian immigration route` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have leave as part of a safe and legal humanitarian immigration route?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do regulation 16(b) and (c) not apply to me because of my status` IF
    `reg 23A(1): a sub-paragraph of paragraph (1) applies to C on the day`
        `I have been granted refugee status or humanitarian protection`
        `I have leave as the dependant of a person granted refugee status or humanitarian protection`
        (`reg 23A(1)(c): C has leave granted by virtue of the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy or the previous scheme` `I have leave under the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy` `I have leave under the previous scheme for locally-employed staff in Afghanistan`)
        `I have discretionary leave as the dependant of a person with leave under the Afghan schemes`
        `I have leave under the Afghan Citizens Resettlement Scheme`
        (`reg 23A(1)(f): the Ukraine paragraph applies` `my leave, abode or exemption` `I was residing in Ukraine immediately before 1 January 2022` `I left Ukraine in connection with the Russian invasion`)
        (`reg 23A(1)(g): the Sudan paragraph applies` `my leave, abode or exemption` `I was residing in Sudan before 15 April 2023` `I left Sudan in connection with the violence`)
        (`reg 23A(1)(h): the Israel and region paragraph applies` `my leave, abode or exemption` `I was residing in Israel or the region immediately before 7 October 2023` `I left Israel or the region in connection with the attack or the violence`)
        (`reg 23A(1B) and (1C): the paragraph still applies on the day` `condition A, B, C and D of paragraph (i) are met` `the day the public information was issued or the evacuation started` `the day`)
        (`reg 23A(1)(j): C has leave as part of a safe and legal humanitarian immigration route` `I have leave as part of a safe and legal humanitarian immigration route` `I have leave under the immigration rules` `I have leave on a discretionary basis outside the immigration rules`)
        (`reg 23A(1B) and (1C): the paragraph still applies on the day` `condition A, B, C and D of paragraph (k) are met` `the day the public information was issued or the evacuation started` `the day`)
        (`reg 23A(1)(l): C has leave as part of a safe and legal humanitarian immigration route` `I have leave as part of a safe and legal humanitarian immigration route` `I have leave under the immigration rules` `I have leave on a discretionary basis outside the immigration rules`)
    WHERE
        `my leave, abode or exemption` MEANS
            `reg 23A(1)(f), (g), (h): C has leave, a right of abode, or needs no leave` `I have leave granted under or outside the immigration rules` `I have a right of abode` `I do not require leave under section 3ZA`
        `condition A, B, C and D of paragraph (i) are met` MEANS
            `reg 23A(1)(i): C met conditions A to D`
                (`reg 23A(1)(i) Condition A: the person was residing in the country or territory when the advice was given or the evacuation arranged` `I was residing outside Great Britain when the Government advised British nationals to leave` `I was residing outside Great Britain when the Government arranged the evacuation of British nationals`)
                (`reg 23A(1)(i) Condition B: the person has left the country or territory` `I have left that country or territory`)
                (`reg 23A(1)(i) Condition C: the person arrived in Great Britain in the first 26 weeks` `the day the public information was issued or the evacuation started` `the day I arrived in Great Britain`)
                (`reg 23A(1)(i) Condition D: the person has the right of abode, needs no leave, or has leave` `I have a right of abode` `I do not require leave under section 3ZA` `I have leave under the immigration rules` `I have leave on a discretionary basis outside the immigration rules`)
        `condition A, B, C and D of paragraph (k) are met` MEANS
            `reg 23A(1)(k): C met conditions A to D`
                (`reg 23A(1)(k) Condition A: the person was residing in the country or territory when the advice was given or the evacuation arranged` `I was residing outside Great Britain when the Government advised British nationals to leave` `I was residing outside Great Britain when the Government arranged the evacuation of British nationals`)
                (`reg 23A(1)(k) Condition B: the person has left the country or territory` `I have left that country or territory`)
                (`reg 23A(1)(k) Condition C: the person arrived in Great Britain in the first 26 weeks` `the day the public information was issued or the evacuation started` `the day I arrived in Great Britain`)
                (`reg 23A(1)(k) Condition D: the person has the right of abode, needs no leave, or has leave` `I have a right of abode` `I do not require leave under section 3ZA` `I have leave under the immigration rules` `I have leave on a discretionary basis outside the immigration rules`)

§§ `The weekly rate (Part 5) and reaching the relevant age (Part 6)`

-- reg 24. The weekly amount of each rate of each component.
@export What is the weekly rate of this component at this rate (reg 24)?
GIVEN `the component` IS A `a component of personal independence payment` @desc Which component? (the daily living component; the mobility component)
      `the rate` IS A `a rate of a component` @desc Which rate? (no rate of the component; the standard rate of the component; the enhanced rate of the component)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the weekly rate of this component at this rate` IS
    `reg 24: the weekly rate, in pounds, of this component at this rate` `the component` `at` `the rate`

-- reg 25. Section 83(1) of the Act stops personal independence payment at the relevant age, but not for a person who was entitled on
-- the day before reaching that age, or who claimed before reaching it, whose claim was undetermined at that age, and would have been
-- awarded a component but for section 83(1).
@export Does section 83(1) of the Act stop my personal independence payment at the relevant age, or does regulation 25 save it (reg 25)?
GIVEN `I have reached the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the relevant age?
      `I was entitled to a component on the day before I reached the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to an award of either or both components on the day before you reached the relevant age?
      `I made a claim before reaching the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a claim for personal independence payment before reaching the relevant age?
      `that claim was not determined before I reached that age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that claim not determined before you reached that age?
      `an award would be made but for section 83(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would an award of either or both components be made in respect of you but for section 83(1) of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does regulation 25 save my personal independence payment from section 83(1)` IF
    `reg 25: section 83(1) of the Act does not apply to C` `I have reached the relevant age` `I was entitled to a component on the day before I reached the relevant age` (`reg 25(b): the claim made before the relevant age qualifies` `I made a claim before reaching the relevant age` `that claim was not determined before I reached that age` `an award would be made but for section 83(1)`)

-- reg 26(1), (2)(a). If I have reached the relevant age and make a new claim after an interval (regulation 15), section 83(1) does not apply.
@export Does regulation 26 save my new claim after an interval from section 83(1) (reg 26(1), (2)(a))?
GIVEN `I have reached the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the relevant age?
      `I make a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15? (see the question about regulation 15)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does regulation 26 save my new claim after an interval from section 83(1)` IF
    `reg 26(2)(a): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply to C` (`reg 26(1): the exceptions of regulation 26(2) apply` `I have reached the relevant age` `I make a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15`)

-- reg 26(2)(c), (d). On a new claim after the relevant age I cannot get a higher rate of the mobility component than the previous award;
-- limited ability gets the standard rate if I had any rate before; severely limited ability gets the previous rate.
@export What rate of the mobility component can I get on my new claim after the relevant age (reg 26(2)(c), (d))?
GIVEN `I have reached the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the relevant age?
      `I make a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15? (see the question about regulation 15)
      `my level of ability to carry out mobility activities on the new claim` IS A `a level of ability to carry out activities` @desc What level of ability to carry out mobility activities is assessed for your new claim? (neither limited ability nor severely limited ability; limited ability; severely limited ability)
      `the rate of the mobility component under my previous award` IS A `a rate of a component` @desc What rate of the mobility component were you entitled to under your previous award? (no rate of the component; the standard rate of the component; the enhanced rate of the component)
GIVETH A MAYBE `a rate of a component`
DECIDE `What rate of the mobility component can I get on my new claim after the relevant age` IS
    `reg 26(2)(c) and (d): the rate of the mobility component C is entitled to on the new claim`
        (`reg 26(1): the exceptions of regulation 26(2) apply` `I have reached the relevant age` `I make a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15`)
        `my level of ability to carry out mobility activities on the new claim`
        `the rate of the mobility component under my previous award`

-- reg 26A(1), (2)(a). The same for a new claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance (regulation 15B).
@export Does regulation 26A save my new claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance from section 83(1) (reg 26A(1), (2)(a))?
GIVEN `I have reached the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the relevant age?
      `I make a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15B(1)? (see the question about regulation 15B)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does regulation 26A save my new claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance from section 83(1)` IF
    `reg 26A(2)(a): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply to C` (`reg 26A(1): the exceptions of regulation 26A(2) apply` `I have reached the relevant age` `I make a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15B(1)`)

-- reg 27(1). When an award that regulation 25 or 26 saved is revised or superseded, section 83(1) does not apply on the revision or supersession.
@export Does section 83(1) not apply when my saved award is revised or superseded (reg 27(1))?
GIVEN `I have reached the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the relevant age?
      `I am entitled to an award under an exception in regulation 25 or 26` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to an award of either or both components pursuant to an exception in regulation 25 or 26?
      `my award falls to be revised or superseded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that award fall to be revised or superseded?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 83(1) not apply when my saved award is revised or superseded` IF
    `reg 27(1): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply on the revision or supersession` `I have reached the relevant age` `I am entitled to an award under an exception in regulation 25 or 26` `my award falls to be revised or superseded`

-- reg 27(2), Secretary of State version. The restrictions of paragraph (3) apply to my mobility component on a supersession for a
-- change of circumstances after the relevant age, or on one I applied for, or the Secretary of State began, after that age.
@export Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded (reg 27(2), Secretary of State version)?
GIVEN `the original award includes an award of the mobility component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your original award include an award of the mobility component?
      `the award is superseded under regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the award superseded under regulation 23 of the Universal Credit, Personal Independence Payment, Jobseeker's Allowance and Employment and Support Allowance (Decisions and Appeals) Regulations 2013?
      `there is a relevant change of circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the supersession for a relevant change of circumstances?
      `the date of the relevant change of circumstances` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did the change of circumstances occur? (ignored if you answered no)
      `the award is superseded under regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the award superseded under regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations?
      `I applied for supersession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply for supersession?
      `the day I applied for supersession` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day did you apply? (ignored if you answered no)
      `the Secretary of State initiated the supersession proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary of State initiate the supersession proceedings?
      `the day the Secretary of State initiated them` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (ignored if you answered no)
      `the day I reached the relevant age` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you reach the relevant age?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded, Secretary of State version` IF
    `reg 27(2) (Secretary of State version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply`
        `the original award includes an award of the mobility component`
        `the award is superseded under regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations`
        `the date of the change, if there is one`
        `the award is superseded under regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations`
        `the day I applied, if I did`
        `the day the Secretary of State initiated them, if they did`
        `the day I reached the relevant age`
    WHERE
        `the date of the change, if there is one` MEANS IF `there is a relevant change of circumstances` THEN JUST `the date of the relevant change of circumstances` ELSE NOTHING
        `the day I applied, if I did` MEANS IF `I applied for supersession` THEN JUST `the day I applied for supersession` ELSE NOTHING
        `the day the Secretary of State initiated them, if they did` MEANS IF `the Secretary of State initiated the supersession proceedings` THEN JUST `the day the Secretary of State initiated them` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 27(2), Scottish Ministers version (the second version of the text; fork F-32).
@export Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded (reg 27(2), Scottish Ministers version)?
GIVEN `the original award includes an award of the mobility component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your original award include an award of the mobility component?
      `the award is superseded under regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the award superseded under regulation 23 of the Universal Credit, Personal Independence Payment, Jobseeker's Allowance and Employment and Support Allowance (Decisions and Appeals) Regulations 2013?
      `there is a relevant change of circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the supersession for a relevant change of circumstances?
      `the date of the relevant change of circumstances` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did the change of circumstances occur? (ignored if you answered no)
      `the award is superseded under regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the award superseded under regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations?
      `I applied for supersession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply for supersession?
      `the day I applied for supersession` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day did you apply? (ignored if you answered no)
      `the Scottish Ministers initiated the supersession proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Scottish Ministers initiate the supersession proceedings?
      `the day the Scottish Ministers initiated them` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (ignored if you answered no)
      `the day I reached the relevant age` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you reach the relevant age?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded, Scottish Ministers version` IF
    `reg 27(2) (Scottish Ministers version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply`
        `the original award includes an award of the mobility component`
        `the award is superseded under regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations`
        `the date of the change, if there is one`
        `the award is superseded under regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations`
        `the day I applied, if I did`
        `the day the Scottish Ministers initiated them, if they did`
        `the day I reached the relevant age`
    WHERE
        `the date of the change, if there is one` MEANS IF `there is a relevant change of circumstances` THEN JUST `the date of the relevant change of circumstances` ELSE NOTHING
        `the day I applied, if I did` MEANS IF `I applied for supersession` THEN JUST `the day I applied for supersession` ELSE NOTHING
        `the day the Scottish Ministers initiated them, if they did` MEANS IF `the Scottish Ministers initiated the supersession proceedings` THEN JUST `the day the Scottish Ministers initiated them` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 27(3). Under the restrictions: a standard rate original award may be replaced only by the standard rate, and only where the
-- entitlement results from substantially the same condition; an enhanced rate original award may be replaced only by the enhanced
-- rate, on the same condition.
@export May the Secretary of State award me this rate of the mobility component in place of my original award (reg 27(3))?
GIVEN `the rate in my original award` IS A `a rate of a component` @desc What rate of the mobility component was in your original award? (no rate of the component; the standard rate of the component; the enhanced rate of the component)
      `the rate I would otherwise be awarded` IS A `a rate of a component` @desc What rate of the mobility component would you otherwise be awarded? (no rate of the component; the standard rate of the component; the enhanced rate of the component)
      `my entitlement results from substantially the same condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your entitlement result from substantially the same condition or conditions for which the mobility component in your original award was made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Secretary of State award me this rate of the mobility component in place of my original award` IS
    `reg 27(3): the Secretary of State may award this rate of the mobility component` `the rate in my original award` `to replace` `the rate I would otherwise be awarded` `with` `my entitlement results from substantially the same condition`

-- reg 27(4). A previous mobility component award that ceased not more than a year before the supersession takes effect counts as the original award.
@export Does my previous mobility component award count as my original award (reg 27(4))?
GIVEN `my original award does not include the mobility component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your original award not include an award of the mobility component?
      `I had a previous award of the mobility component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a previous award of the mobility component?
      `the day my entitlement under the previous award ceased` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your entitlement under the previous award cease?
      `the date the supersession takes or would take effect` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the supersession take, or would it take, effect?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my previous mobility component award count as my original award` IF
    `reg 27(4): entitlement under the previous award is treated as if it were under the original award` `my original award does not include the mobility component` `I had a previous award of the mobility component` `the day my entitlement under the previous award ceased` `the date the supersession takes or would take effect`

§§ `Payment while I am in a care home, a hospital or custody (Part 7)`

-- reg 32(2)(a). A period of residence begins on the day after the day I enter the care home, hospital or similar institution, or begin custody.
@export On what day does my period of residence begin (reg 32(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the day I enter the care home, hospital or similar institution or begin custody` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you enter a care home, hospital or similar institution, or begin imprisonment or detention in legal custody?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my period of residence begin` IS
    `reg 32(2)(a): the first day of the period of residence` `the day I enter the care home, hospital or similar institution or begin custody`

-- reg 32(2)(b), (3). It ends on the day before the day I leave (or custody ends), unless another period of residence follows immediately,
-- in which case the earlier period ends on the day I leave.
@export On what day does my period of residence end (reg 32(2)(b), (3))?
GIVEN `the day I leave or my custody ends` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you leave the care home, hospital or similar institution, or does your imprisonment or detention end?
      `I start another period of residence immediately following` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you start another period of residence immediately after?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my period of residence end` IS
    `reg 32(2)(b) and (3): the last day of the period of residence` `the day I leave or my custody ends` `with` `I start another period of residence immediately following`

-- reg 32(1). I am in a period of residence if I meet the care home condition, the hospital condition or I am in custody.
@export Am I in a period of residence (reg 32(1))?
GIVEN `I meet the condition in section 85(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the condition in section 85(2) of the Act (care home)? (see the question about regulation 28(2))
      `I meet the condition in section 86(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the condition in section 86(2) of the Act (hospital in-patient)? (see the question about regulation 29(2))
      `I am undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in a period of residence` IF
    `reg 32(1): C is in a period of residence` `I meet the condition in section 85(2) of the Act` `I meet the condition in section 86(2) of the Act` `I am undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody`

-- reg 32(4), (5). Distinct periods of residence separated by not more than 28 days (a year, where both are periods to which section 87
-- applies) make one continuous period. The seat takes up to three periods in date order.
@export How many days of residence have I accumulated in my continuous period up to this day (reg 32(4), (5))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking?
      `both periods are periods to which section 87 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each of your periods of residence a period to which section 87 of the Act (custody) applies?
      `the day I entered for my first period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you enter, or begin custody, for your first period of residence?
      `the day I left from my first period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you leave, or did custody end, for your first period? (the day you are asking about, if you have not yet left)
      `another period follows my first immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another period of residence follow your first immediately?
      `I have a second period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a second period of residence?
      `the day I entered for my second period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you enter, or begin custody, for your second period? (ignored if you have none)
      `the day I left from my second period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you leave, or did custody end, for your second period? (ignored if you have none)
      `another period follows my second immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another period follow your second immediately? (ignored if you have none)
      `I have a third period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a third period of residence?
      `the day I entered for my third period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you enter, or begin custody, for your third period? (ignored if you have none)
      `the day I left from my third period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you leave, or did custody end, for your third period? (ignored if you have none)
      `another period follows my third immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another period follow your third immediately? (ignored if you have none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of residence have I accumulated in my continuous period up to this day` IS
    `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` `my periods` `up to` `the day` `with` `both periods are periods to which section 87 applies`
    WHERE
        `my periods` MEANS append (LIST `my first period`) (append (IF `I have a second period` THEN LIST `my second period` ELSE EMPTY) (IF `I have a third period` THEN LIST `my third period` ELSE EMPTY))
        `my first period` MEANS `reg 32(2) and (3): the period of residence from entry to leaving` `the day I entered for my first period` `to` `the day I left from my first period` `with` `another period follows my first immediately`
        `my second period` MEANS `reg 32(2) and (3): the period of residence from entry to leaving` `the day I entered for my second period` `to` `the day I left from my second period` `with` `another period follows my second immediately`
        `my third period` MEANS `reg 32(2) and (3): the period of residence from entry to leaving` `the day I entered for my third period` `to` `the day I left from my third period` `with` `another period follows my third immediately`

-- reg 28(2). I meet the care home condition if qualifying services are provided to me in a care home and the costs are borne out of public
-- or local funds under a specified enactment.
@export Do I meet the care home condition of section 85(2) of the Act (reg 28(2))?
GIVEN `qualifying services are provided to me in a care home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are qualifying services provided to you in a care home?
      `the costs of those services are borne out of public or local funds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the costs of those services borne out of public or local funds under an enactment?
      `the enactment` IS AN `an enactment under which qualifying services may be provided` @desc Under which enactment are the costs borne? (Part 3 of the National Assistance Act 1948; sections 59 and 59A of the Social Work (Scotland) Act 1968; the Mental Health Act 1983; the Community Care and Health (Scotland) Act 2002; the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003; section 57 of the Health and Social Care Act 2001; Part 1 of the Care Act 2014; Part 4 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014; any other enactment relating to persons under a disability or to young persons or to education or training; section 485 of the Education Act 1996; section 14 of the Education Act 2002; section 49 or section 73 of the Education (Scotland) Act 1980; section 65 of the Further and Higher Education Act 1992; section 4 or section 11 of the Further and Higher Education (Scotland) Act 2005; section 22 of the Teaching and Higher Education Act 1998; section 39 or section 40 of the Higher Education and Research Act 2017; an enactment of some other kind)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the care home condition of section 85(2) of the Act` IF
    `reg 28(2): C meets the condition in section 85(2) of the Act` `qualifying services are provided to me in a care home` `the costs of those services are borne out of public or local funds` `the enactment`

-- reg 28(3), (4). Regulation 28(1) does not apply to me, if I am under 18 and one of the children in need or looked-after provisions applies and
-- the local authority places me in a private dwelling; or if I am accommodated outside the United Kingdom at a local authority's cost.
@export Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because of my age and placement (reg 28(3), (4))?
GIVEN `I have not reached the age of 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under the age of 18?
      `section 17(10)(b) of the Children Act 1989 or section 93(4)(a)(ii) of the 1995 Act applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 17(10)(b) of the Children Act 1989 or section 93(4)(a)(ii) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 apply to you, because your health is likely to be significantly impaired, or further impaired, without the provision of services?
      `section 17(10)(c) of the Children Act 1989 or section 93(4)(a)(iii) of the 1995 Act applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 17(10)(c) of the Children Act 1989 or section 93(4)(a)(iii) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 apply to you?
      `section 37, 38 or 42 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 37, 38 or 42 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 apply to you?
      `the local authority looking after me places me in a private dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the local authority looking after you place you in a private dwelling with a family, or with a relative of yours, or with some other suitable person?
      `I am accommodated outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you accommodated outside the United Kingdom?
      `the costs are borne by a local authority under the Education Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the costs of any qualifying services borne wholly or partly by a local authority pursuant to their powers under section 320 of the Education Act 1996 or section 25 of the Education (Additional Support for Learning) (Scotland) Act 2004?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because of my age and placement` IF
    `reg 28(3): paragraph (1) does not apply to C`
        (`reg 28(3)(a), (aa) and (4): the local authority placement exception applies`
            (`reg 28(3)(a): C is a person under 18 to whom the children in need provisions apply` `I have not reached the age of 18` `section 17(10)(b) of the Children Act 1989 or section 93(4)(a)(ii) of the 1995 Act applies to me` `section 17(10)(c) of the Children Act 1989 or section 93(4)(a)(iii) of the 1995 Act applies to me`)
            `section 37, 38 or 42 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 applies to me`
            `the local authority looking after me places me in a private dwelling`)
        (`reg 28(3)(b): C is accommodated outside the United Kingdom at a local authority's cost` `I am accommodated outside the United Kingdom` `the costs are borne by a local authority under the Education Acts`)

-- reg 30(1), (2). Payment goes on for the first 28 days of a continuous period of residence, and for any run of consecutive days beginning
-- with the day my entitlement commenced on which I meet the condition.
@export Does my payment go on because this day is among the first 28 days (reg 30(1), (2))?
GIVEN `I am in a period of residence on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in a period of residence on the day?
      `the days of residence in my continuous period up to the day` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many days of residence are there in your continuous period up to and including the day? (see the question about reg 32(4); ignored if you answered no)
      `the day falls in the run beginning with the day my entitlement commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the day fall in an unbroken run of days, beginning with the day your entitlement to personal independence payment commenced, on which you have met the condition?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my payment go on because this day is among the first 28 days` IF
    `reg 30(1) and (2): payment goes on because the day is among the first 28 days` `my days of residence, if I am in a period` `the day falls in the run beginning with the day my entitlement commenced`
    WHERE
        `my days of residence, if I am in a period` MEANS IF `I am in a period of residence on the day` THEN JUST `the days of residence in my continuous period up to the day` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 30(4). A hospice is a hospital or other institution whose primary function is palliative care for persons with a progressive disease in
-- its final stages, other than a health service hospital in England, Wales or Scotland, a Defence Council hospital, or a similar institution.
@export Is the place where I live a hospice (reg 30(4))?
GIVEN `its primary function is palliative care for persons with a progressive disease in its final stages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its primary function to provide palliative care for persons resident there who are suffering from a progressive disease in its final stages?
      `it is a health service hospital in England` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a health service hospital in England?
      `it is a hospital in Wales vested in an NHS trust, a Local Health Board or the Welsh Ministers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a hospital in Wales vested in an NHS trust, a Local Health Board or the Welsh Ministers for the purpose of functions under the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006?
      `it is a health service hospital in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a health service hospital in Scotland?
      `it is a hospital maintained by the Defence Council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a hospital maintained by the Defence Council?
      `it is similar to a hospital mentioned above` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it similar to a hospital mentioned in any of the preceding questions?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the place where I live a hospice` IF
    `reg 30(4): the institution is a hospice` `its primary function is palliative care for persons with a progressive disease in its final stages` `it is a health service hospital in England` `it is a hospital in Wales vested in an NHS trust, a Local Health Board or the Welsh Ministers` `it is a health service hospital in Scotland` `it is a hospital maintained by the Defence Council` `it is similar to a hospital mentioned above`

-- reg 30(3). Regulations 28 and 29 do not apply to me if I live in a hospice, am terminally ill, and the Secretary of State has been informed.
@export Do regulations 28 and 29 not apply to me because I am terminally ill in a hospice (reg 30(3))?
GIVEN `I am residing in a hospice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you residing in a hospice? (see the question about regulation 30(4))
      `I am terminally ill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you terminally ill (within the meaning of section 82 of the Act)?
      `the Secretary of State has been informed on a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State been informed that you are terminally ill on a claim for personal independence payment?
      `the Secretary of State has been informed on an application for revision or supersession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State been informed that you are terminally ill on an application for a revision or a supersession of an award?
      `the Secretary of State has been informed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State been informed in writing, in connection with an award of, or a claim for, or an application for a revision or a supersession of an award of, personal independence payment, that you are terminally ill?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do regulations 28 and 29 not apply to me because I am terminally ill in a hospice` IF
    `reg 30(3): regulation 28 or 29 does not apply because C is terminally ill in a hospice` `I am residing in a hospice` `I am terminally ill` `the Secretary of State has been informed on a claim` `the Secretary of State has been informed on an application for revision or supersession` `the Secretary of State has been informed in writing`

-- reg 30(5). Regulation 28(1) does not apply where the total cost of the qualifying services is met from private means.
@export Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because the whole cost is met from private means (reg 30(5))?
GIVEN `the total cost is met out of my own resources` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the total cost of the qualifying services met out of your own resources?
      `the total cost is met partly out of my resources and partly with assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the total cost met partly out of your own resources and partly with assistance from another person or a charity?
      `the total cost is met on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the total cost met on your behalf by another person or a charity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because the whole cost is met from private means` IF
    `reg 30(5): regulation 28(1) does not apply because the total cost is met from private means` `the total cost is met out of my own resources` `the total cost is met partly out of my resources and partly with assistance` `the total cost is met on my behalf`

-- reg 28(1). No amount attributable to the daily living component is payable for a period when I meet the care home condition, subject to
-- regulation 28(3) and regulation 30.
@export Is an amount attributable to my daily living component payable for this day while I am in a care home (reg 28(1))?
GIVEN `I meet the condition in section 85(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the care home condition of section 85(2) of the Act? (see the question about regulation 28(2))
      `regulation 28(3) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 28(3) mean regulation 28(1) does not apply to you? (see the question about regulation 28(3))
      `payment goes on because the day is among the first 28 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your payment go on because the day is among the first 28 days? (see the question about regulation 30(1), (2))
      `regulation 30(3) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 30(3) mean regulations 28 and 29 do not apply to you? (see the question about regulation 30(3))
      `regulation 30(5) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 30(5) mean regulation 28(1) does not apply to you? (see the question about regulation 30(5))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an amount attributable to my daily living component payable for this day while I am in a care home` IF
    `reg 28(1): an amount attributable to the daily living component is payable for the day` `I meet the condition in section 85(2) of the Act` `regulation 28(3) applies to me` `payment goes on because the day is among the first 28 days` `regulation 30(3) applies to me` `regulation 30(5) applies to me`

-- reg 29(2). I meet the hospital in-patient condition of section 86(2) if I am undergoing treatment as an in-patient in a specified type of institution.
@export Do I meet the hospital in-patient condition of section 86(2) of the Act (reg 29(2))?
GIVEN `I am undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient?
      `the institution` IS AN `an institution in which C is an in-patient` @desc Which kind of institution are you in? (a hospital or similar institution under the National Health Service Act 2006; under the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006; under the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978; maintained or administered by the Defence Council; some other institution)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the hospital in-patient condition of section 86(2) of the Act` IF
    `reg 29(2): the costs of treatment, accommodation or related services are borne out of public funds` `I am undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient` `the institution`

-- reg 29(3). Regulation 29 does not apply to me if I was under 18 on the day I entered the hospital to begin my current period as an in-patient.
@export Does regulation 29 not apply to me because I was under 18 when I entered hospital (reg 29(3))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day I entered the hospital to begin my current period as an in-patient` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you enter the hospital or similar institution to begin your current period as an in-patient?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does regulation 29 not apply to me because I was under 18 when I entered hospital` IF
    `reg 29(3): regulation 29 does not apply because C was under 18 on the day of entry` `my date of birth` `the day I entered the hospital to begin my current period as an in-patient`

-- reg 29(1). No amount attributable to either component is payable for a period when I meet the hospital in-patient condition, subject to regulation 29(3) and regulation 30.
@export Is an amount attributable to my components payable for this day while I am in hospital (reg 29(1))?
GIVEN `I meet the condition in section 86(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the hospital in-patient condition of section 86(2) of the Act? (see the question about regulation 29(2))
      `regulation 29(3) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 29(3) mean regulation 29 does not apply to you? (see the question about regulation 29(3))
      `payment goes on because the day is among the first 28 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your payment go on because the day is among the first 28 days? (see the question about regulation 30(1), (2))
      `regulation 30(3) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 30(3) mean regulations 28 and 29 do not apply to you? (see the question about regulation 30(3))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an amount attributable to my components payable for this day while I am in hospital` IF
    `reg 29(1): an amount attributable to either component is payable for the day` `I meet the condition in section 86(2) of the Act` `regulation 29(3) applies to me` `payment goes on because the day is among the first 28 days` `regulation 30(3) applies to me`

-- reg 31(1), (2). Section 87 stops payment while I am a person to whom it applies, but not for the first 28 days of a period.
@export Does my payment go on in custody because this day is among the first 28 days (reg 31(1), (2))?
GIVEN `I am in a period of residence on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in a period of residence on the day?
      `the days of residence in my continuous period up to the day` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many days of residence are there in your continuous period up to and including the day? (see the question about reg 32(4); ignored if you answered no)
      `the day falls in the run beginning with the day my entitlement commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the day fall in an unbroken run of days, beginning with the day your entitlement commenced, on which section 87 has applied to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my payment go on in custody because this day is among the first 28 days` IF
    `reg 31(1) and (2): section 87 does not apply because the day is among the first 28 days` `my days of residence, if I am in a period` `the day falls in the run beginning with the day my entitlement commenced`
    WHERE
        `my days of residence, if I am in a period` MEANS IF `I am in a period of residence on the day` THEN JUST `the days of residence in my continuous period up to the day` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 31(5)(a). A hospital or similar institution is a place, not a prison, detention centre, young offenders institution or remand centre, where persons
-- suffering from mental disorder are or may be received for care or treatment.
@export Is the place where I am detained a hospital or similar institution (reg 31(5)(a))?
GIVEN `persons suffering from mental disorder are or may be received there for care or treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are persons suffering from mental disorder received there, or may they be received there, for care or treatment?
      `the place is a prison, a detention centre, a young offenders institution or a remand centre` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place a prison, a detention centre, a young offenders institution or a remand centre?
      `the place is at or in a prison, a detention centre, a young offenders institution or a remand centre` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place at or in a prison, a detention centre, a young offenders institution or a remand centre?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the place where I am detained a hospital or similar institution` IF
    `reg 31(5)(a): the place is a hospital or similar institution` `persons suffering from mental disorder are or may be received there for care or treatment` `the place is a prison, a detention centre, a young offenders institution or a remand centre` `the place is at or in a prison, a detention centre, a young offenders institution or a remand centre`

-- reg 31(5)(b). Criminal proceedings against me are deemed concluded once I am found insane in them so that I cannot be tried or the trial cannot proceed.
@export Are the criminal proceedings against me deemed concluded (reg 31(5)(b))?
GIVEN `I have been found insane in those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been found insane in those proceedings?
      `I cannot be tried or the trial cannot proceed as a result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the effect of that finding that you cannot be tried or that the trial cannot proceed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the criminal proceedings against me deemed concluded` IF
    `reg 31(5)(b): the criminal proceedings are deemed to be concluded` `I have been found insane in those proceedings` `I cannot be tried or the trial cannot proceed as a result`

-- reg 31(4). I satisfy a condition of paragraph (4) if I am detained under section 45A or 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983 on or before my certified release
-- date, or under section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995 or section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003.
@export Do I satisfy one of the conditions of regulation 31(4)?
GIVEN `I am detained under section 45A or section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you detained under section 45A of the Mental Health Act 1983 or section 47 of that Act?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking?
      `the Secretary of State has certified my release date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State certified a release date for you, within the meaning of section 50(3) of that Act?
      `my certified release date` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is your certified release date? (ignored if you answered no)
      `I am being detained under section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you being detained under section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995 (hospital direction)?
      `I am being detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you being detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I satisfy one of the conditions of regulation 31(4)` IF
    `reg 31(4): C satisfies one of the conditions` `I am detained under section 45A or section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` `the day` `my release date, if certified` `I am being detained under section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995` `I am being detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003`
    WHERE
        `my release date, if certified` MEANS IF `the Secretary of State has certified my release date` THEN JUST `my certified release date` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 31(3). After my criminal proceedings conclude, section 87 does not apply to me while I am detained in a hospital in Great Britain, unless regulation 31(4) applies.
@export Does section 87 not apply to me because my criminal proceedings concluded and I am detained in hospital (reg 31(3))?
GIVEN `I am detained in a hospital or similar institution in Great Britain as a person suffering from mental disorder as a result of criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you detained in a hospital or similar institution in Great Britain as a person suffering from mental disorder as a result of criminal proceedings?
      `the criminal proceedings have concluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the criminal proceedings concluded? (see the question about regulation 31(5)(b))
      `I satisfy one of the conditions in paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy one of the conditions in regulation 31(4)? (see the question about that)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 87 not apply to me because my criminal proceedings concluded and I am detained in hospital` IF
    `reg 31(3): section 87 does not apply because the criminal proceedings concluded` `I am detained in a hospital or similar institution in Great Britain as a person suffering from mental disorder as a result of criminal proceedings` `the criminal proceedings have concluded` `I satisfy one of the conditions in paragraph (4)`

-- reg 31(6). Section 87 does not apply to me while I am in custody outside Great Britain if, in similar circumstances in Great Britain, regulation 31 would have excepted me.
@export Does section 87 not apply to me because I am in custody outside Great Britain (reg 31(6))?
GIVEN `I am undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody outside Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody outside Great Britain?
      `in similar circumstances in Great Britain I would have been excepted by a provision of regulation 31` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In similar circumstances in Great Britain, would you have been excepted from the application of section 87 by a provision of regulation 31?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 87 not apply to me because I am in custody outside Great Britain` IF
    `reg 31(6): section 87 does not apply because the custody is outside Great Britain` `I am undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody outside Great Britain` `in similar circumstances in Great Britain I would have been excepted by a provision of regulation 31`

-- reg 31. An amount of personal independence payment is payable for the day unless section 87 applies to me and no exception of regulation 31 applies.
@export Is an amount of personal independence payment payable for this day while I am in custody (reg 31)?
GIVEN `section 87 of the Act applies to me on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 87 of the Act apply to you on the day?
      `payment goes on because the day is among the first 28 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your payment go on because the day is among the first 28 days? (see the question about regulation 31(1), (2))
      `regulation 31(3) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 31(3) mean section 87 does not apply to you? (see the question about regulation 31(3))
      `regulation 31(6) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 31(6) mean section 87 does not apply to you? (see the question about regulation 31(6))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an amount of personal independence payment payable for this day while I am in custody` IF
    `reg 31: an amount of personal independence payment is payable for the day` `section 87 of the Act applies to me on the day` `payment goes on because the day is among the first 28 days` `regulation 31(3) applies to me` `regulation 31(6) applies to me`
